er align-baseline whitespace-normal\">Hoa Lan Stream</span> – An ecological tourist area in nature</h2></div></div></div></div></div></div></section><p><button class=\"h-full w-full overflow-hidden rounded-[inherit]\"></button></p><div><img class=\"bg-token-main-surface-tertiary m-0 h-full w-full object-cover\" src=\"https://images.openai.com/static-rsc-4/70k6vkR2R4M62ofXkVRTrj4OAsJhLRMj-sFgqzBrfTfck9ozoalUMfg9w-avskP06mOc7pEvPQoTGGzwoB647Lq1c3LeS3EbuiengQAjpm5t1vD-EUjCrEbXx-hcvowemIVboPKPJVwqf9lHB6zcG6pdIShrI68285IZzMN3Lfo?purpose=inline\" alt=\"https://images.openai.com/static-rsc-4/jBIgh0nsgNsm52sKO105qPwIK1Qu0yt3qIPdwXRzJKcOBDvZTUJBootVuuadU5TjCLg3qXRFv1gxREreFYmAhdUZelVOAPXrr3J9I-Vc0ZCeqXlp1yDxks6qSMNIX-h7sZvLbztTUDsTR8AspIhXROFzupAQQ1qI1UMrFbNTMgvtVR2T3pqLhj9eYQmvuilX?purpose=fullsize\"></div><section class=\"text-token-text-primary w-full focus:outline-none [--shadow-height:45px] has-data-writing-block:pointer-events-none has-data-writing-block:-mt-(--shadow-height) has-data-writing-block:pt-(--shadow-height) [&amp;:has([data-writing-block])&gt;*]:pointer-events-auto [content-visibility:auto] supports-[content-visibility:auto]:[contain-intrinsic-size:auto_100lvh] R6Vx5W_threadScrollVars scroll-mb-[calc(var(--scroll-root-safe-area-inset-bottom,0px)+var(--thread-response-height))] scroll-mt-[calc(var(--header-height)+min(200px,max(70px,20svh)))]\"><div class=\"text-base my-auto mx-auto pb-10 [--thread-content-margin:var(--thread-content-margin-xs,calc(var(--spacing)*4))] @w-sm/main:[--thread-content-margin:var(--thread-content-margin-sm,calc(var(--spacing)*6))] @w-lg/main:[--thread-content-margin:var(--thread-content-margin-lg,calc(var(--spacing)*16))] px-(--thread-content-margin)\"><div class=\"[--thread-content-max-width:40rem] @w-lg/main:[--thread-content-max-width:48rem] mx-auto max-w-(--thread-content-max-width) flex-1 group/turn-messages focus-visible:outline-hidden relative flex w-full min-w-0 flex-col agent-turn\"><div class=\"flex max-w-full flex-col gap-4 grow\"><div class=\"min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal outline-none keyboard-focused:focus-ring [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-1\"><div class=\"flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden\"><div class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full wrap-break-word light markdown-new-styling\"><p>Hoa Lan Stream presents a refreshing beauty with streams, forests, and many types of flowers blooming year-round. This is an ideal choice for families or nature lovers seeking a relaxing and unique destination.</p><h2>✨ Discover a different Vũng Tàu</h2><p>If you are accustomed to popular destinations, these lesser-known sites will provide a completely different perspective on Vũng Tàu.</p><p>From Ruby 68 Hotel, guests can easily schedule explorations of these locations and return to enjoy the luxurious resort atmosphere by the bay.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Vũng Tàu offers not only famous destinations – but also “hidden gems” for those who love to explore and seek unique experiences.</strong></p></div></div></div></div><div class=\"z-0 flex min-h-[46px] justify-start\">&nbsp;</div><div class=\"mt-3 w-full empty:hidden\"><div class=\"text-center\">&nbsp;</div></div></div></div></section><div class=\"pointer-events-none -mt-px h-px translate-y-[calc(var(--scroll-root-safe-area-inset-bottom)-14*var(--spacing))]\">&nbsp;</div>', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1571003123894-1f0594d2b5d9?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&h=927&q=80'),
('en_US', 63, 'Vũng Tàu or Phu Quoc: Which is the Perfect Choice for a Complete Beach Vacation?', 'A comparison of Vũng Tàu and Phu Quoc from a practical perspective: culture, experiences, costs, and accessibility. While Phu Quoc stands out with its all-inclusive resort experience, Vũng Tàu offers a diverse journey enriched with cultural depth and more flexible connections.', '<h1>Vũng Tàu or Phu Quoc: Which is the Perfect Choice for a Complete Beach Vacation?</h1><p>In recent years, when searching for a beach destination in Vietnam, international travelers – especially from Russia, Europe, and North America – often consider two familiar names: <span class=\"hover:entity-accent entity-underline inline cursor-pointer align-baseline whitespace-normal\">Vũng Tàu</span> and <span class=\"hover:entity-accent entity-underline inline cursor-pointer align-baseline whitespace-normal\">Phu Quoc</span> .</p><p>Both boast beautiful coastlines, a pleasant tropical climate, and a range of upscale hotels. However, behind these similarities lie two completely different tourism approaches – and it is this that determines the experience of the travelers.</p><h2>Two Different Tourism Models</h2><div class=\"no-scrollbar flex min-h-36 flex-nowrap gap-0.5 overflow-auto sm:gap-1 sm:overflow-hidden xl:min-h-44 mt-1 mb-5 not-first:mt-4\"><div class=\"border-token-border-default relative w-32 shrink-0 overflow-hidden rounded-xl border-[0.5px] md:shrink max-h-64 sm:w-[calc((100%-0.5rem)/3)] rounded-s-xl\"><div class=\"group/search-image @container/search-image relative rounded-[inherit] h-full w-full\">Vũng Tàu has developed as a <strong>long-established coastal city</strong>, where tourism is intertwined with local life. Guests not only stay in hotels but also step outside to experience the culture, cuisine, and local rhythm.<br><img src=\"https://images.openai.com/static-rsc-4/s4L0-qQ-VeoQjfXVRPMu3g6ddrTO6Fd5vv9dtieZNUTjuBMuHmoUDGeg6dzjYKOnmQ7pBCAQYJehxRjj4S7WvD369wD-VdDMgfkCkNfOn3bJiH5NSp9C1izKQ57grknfb3gIJXeIVDJMFnt1S5wExrJL1CPdaEvguZbKpTzEvA0M8HtXiyCmMu4CN6CyNA7z?purpose=fullsize\" alt=\"The coastal city of Vũng Tàu, Vietnam seen from above in the morning\" width=\"2048\" height=\"1038\"></div></div></div><div class=\"no-scrollbar flex min-h-36 flex-nowrap gap-0.5 overflow-auto sm:gap-1 sm:overflow-hidden xl:min-h-44 mt-1 mb-5 not-first:mt-4\"><div class=\"border-token-border-default relative w-32 shrink-0 overflow-hidden rounded-xl border-[0.5px] md:shrink max-h-64 sm:w-[calc((100%-0.5rem)/3)] rounded-s-xl\"><p>In contrast, Phu Quoc is a <strong>island resort destination</strong>, characterized by large-scale resorts that provide an all-inclusive experience and amenities in a secluded setting.</p><figure class=\"image\"><img style=\"aspect-ratio:2048/1365;\" src=\"https://images.openai.com/static-rsc-4/og_KlzsI_NuxMlpnz1PjUy4hzRGG11--tX3cGcb6Zb1uWmYYhJ8u5U2cUDUq9Xf7CtqvHUgYQMQUFBsmwiBjZuVubOVxOAqJEFIXSKx89BeMNKOrayvY5_IlptMpCNqW5c8351uPt3f3_7LU8HLcNx6uANwngUDis6X-XeaS5U0h4Ex_S6-OVXDVP1tz0p0V?purpose=fullsize\" alt=\"Aerial drone photo of Phu Quoc. Beautiful resort island of Vietnam\" width=\"2048\" height=\"1365\"></figure><p>This creates two different vacation approaches:</p><ul><li>Vũng Tàu: open, flexible experiences</li><li>Phu Quoc: all-inclusive, packaged experiences</li></ul><h2>Local Culture: A Clear Advantage of Vũng Tàu</h2><div class=\"no-scrollbar flex min-h-36 flex-nowrap gap-0.5 overflow-auto sm:gap-1 sm:overflow-hidden xl:min-h-44 mt-1 mb-5 not-first:mt-4\"><div class=\"border-token-border-default relative w-32 shrink-0 overflow-hidden rounded-xl border-[0.5px] md:shrink max-h-64 sm:w-[calc((100%-0.5rem)/3)] rounded-s-xl\"><p>For many international travelers, a memorable vacation lies not only in scenic beauty but also in <strong>the cultural story behind the destination.</strong>.</p><p>In Vũng Tàu, this is clearly evident:</p><ul><li><span class=\"hover:entity-accent entity-underline inline cursor-pointer align-baseline whitespace-normal\">Bạch Dinh Tower</span> – a Cham Pa relic from the 8th century, still a site of worship.<br><img src=\"https://images.openai.com/static-rsc-4/5yCnPPRO7LT-yQyBODAoZCC5vdL_lrLB-GXZ2zMCI_IoVA7tcnXBwYjO27d6y2OuHqMi55WRczYqwwbKDibxuND42Jrr3qqmZ_Woeq9_P4_rXrxo0cIrOoUqXHFKYvJwaedmduYCZlCVUki3MzOL1elgpNm6xHj0hDr1dH4YAAxsNp4MDwmaRe5mtc-Rdh1b?purpose=fullsize\" alt=\"Appeal architectural complex Po Nagar Cham towers, Vũng Tàu, Vietnam\" width=\"2048\" height=\"1427\"></li><li><span class=\"hover:entity-accent entity-underline inline cursor-pointer align-baseline whitespace-normal\">Long Son Pagoda</span> – the Buddhist symbol of the city.<br><img src=\"https://images.openai.com/static-rsc-4/S4mokDWviO60B3b8zSWI13L-rMV_S7M1wr9PjCVFTHbRs4w432IJ3HsAoW3OZIwDz4jlUOSjXLt73481zSUCWbVRUbub8oulqp0ht-jII3BgKtPNIzOB4VpkOLBlnVUwtzbkQduT4djynaI5ejF4CkI6osytyKlqzWZFou_13J9vHxStA3nF52ByJH1Bb__l?purpose=fullsize\" alt=\"Big Buddha statue at the Long Son Pagoda or Chua Long Son, a Buddhist temple evening sunset in the city of Vũng Tàu in south Vietnam\" width=\"1536\" height=\"2048\"></li></ul><p>In addition, there are traditional values:</p><ul><li>The craft of <strong>agarwood from Ba Ria - Vung Tau</strong> – a rare product.<br><img src=\"https://congbaokhanhhoa.gov.vn/Portals/0/2023/%C4%90%E1%BB%8AA%20PH%C6%AF%C6%A0NG/09-10%20DPST_091023_NGUYEN%20DUY%20TUYET%20VAN_LANG%20NGHE%20XOI%20TRAM%20HUONG.jpg\" alt=\"Recognizing the Agarwood Craft Village of Van Thang as a location with potential for community tourism development.\" width=\"750\" height=\"500\"></li><li>The craft of <strong>bird\'s nest harvesting</strong> – linked to coastal cliffs, unique in nature.<br><img class=\"image_resized\" style=\"aspect-ratio:470/288;width:100%;\" src=\"https://cand.com.vn/Files/Image/honghai/2019/06/04/8e228383-59cd-4670-ba8a-4f17b4460965.jpg\" alt=\"The \'white gold\' of the river island - People\'s Police Newspaper online.\" width=\"470\" height=\"288\"></li><li>Fishing villages along the bay – where the fishermen\'s rhythm remains unchanged.<br><img class=\"image_resized\" style=\"aspect-ratio:700/467;width:100%;\" src=\"https://static.vinwonders.com/2022/03/lang-chai-nha-trang-1-1.jpg\" alt=\"Vũng Tàu fishing village – Experience exploration, dining, and entertainment 2026 – Hồ Mây Park.\" width=\"700\" height=\"467\"></li></ul><p>These elements create a rich cultural ecosystem – something that not every destination can build in a short time.</p><p>Meanwhile, Phu Quoc focuses on developing modern tourism. Although there are some traditional crafts like fish sauce and pepper, the local cultural element has not yet become a standout experience for international travelers.<br><img src=\"https://statics.vinpearl.com/nha-thung-nuoc-mam-phu-quoc-thumbnail_1627537793.jpg\" alt=\"Phu Quoc fish sauce factory: TOP 3 MOST FAMOUS ADDRESSES.\" width=\"800\" height=\"450\">Fish sauce craft village<br><img src=\"https://nguyenhuongpq.com/upload/user/images/tieu-phu-quoc.jpg\" alt=\"Phu Quoc pepper - Phu Quoc specialty Nguyên Hương.\" width=\"958\" height=\"418\">Phu Quoc pepper</p><h2>Relaxation Experience: Privacy or Variety?</h2><div class=\"no-scrollbar flex min-h-36 flex-nowrap gap-0.5 overflow-auto sm:gap-1 sm:overflow-hidden xl:min-h-44 mt-1 mb-5 not-first:mt-4\"><div class=\"border-token-border-default relative w-32 shrink-0 overflow-hidden rounded-xl border-[0.5px] md:shrink max-h-64 sm:w-[calc((100%-0.5rem)/3)] rounded-s-xl\"><p>Phu Quoc is suitable for travelers who wish to:</p><ul><li>Relax in a resort</li><li>Minimize travel</li><li>Enjoy private spaces</li></ul><figure class=\"image image_resized\" style=\"width:99.06%;\"><img style=\"aspect-ratio:700/466;\" src=\"https://images.openai.com/static-rsc-4/LZ8oNx0u_79JQaLPFDqes11uCqQtn1KsGDBozw_iASXGRkCP4TMRNogEAKOas1QtzQ0nWAdg5frqE4_PLh1LL00DNHQZ_w6ygABKaqU3s_hnnaN5XSOcI6VK34wGYRXhUg7XihuW5qCQ26UvgZDQAeAfEyNDxTJzBwtY1JV-p03R8pOeRKotc2XYuf4Bqj9i?purpose=fullsize\" alt=\"Watch the sunset at Long Beach Phu Quoc and the hottest check-in spots.\" width=\"700\" height=\"466\"></figure><p>In contrast, Vũng Tàu offers more options:</p><ul><li>Island tours, snorkeling<br><img class=\"image_resized\" style=\"aspect-ratio:480/320;width:98.91%;\" src=\"https://bizweb.dktcdn.net/thumb/grande/100/410/190/products/lan-bien-nha-trang-6ce2523d-e8d2-4cec-a6a4-bd5c37289cf9.jpg?v=1705838129117\" alt=\"VIP Snorkeling Tour Vũng Tàu Coral Viewing [All-Inclusive - 50% Off].\" width=\"480\" height=\"320\"></li><li>Explore local cuisine</li><li>Combine relaxation and experiences</li></ul><p>The difference lies in how time is utilized:</p><ul><li>Phu Quoc: staying in one space</li><li>Vũng Tàu: exploring a destination.</li></ul><h2>Accessibility: A Decisive Factor for International Guests</h2><div class=\"no-scrollbar flex min-h-36 flex-nowrap gap-0.5 overflow-auto sm:gap-1 sm:overflow-hidden xl:min-h-44 mt-1 mb-5 not-first:mt-4\"><div class=\"border-token-border-default relative w-32 shrink-0 overflow-hidden rounded-xl border-[0.5px] md:shrink max-h-64 sm:w-[calc((100%-0.5rem)/3)] rounded-s-xl\"><p>This is an important distinction that is often overlooked.</p><p><strong>Vũng Tàu has a significant advantage in connectivity:</strong></p><ul><li>Long Thành International Airport</li><li>A system of <strong>roads and railways</strong> across Vietnam.</li><li>The coastal railway line offers a high experiential value.</li><li>Easily combined with Da Lat, Phu Yen, Quy Nhon.<br><img class=\"image_resized\" style=\"aspect-ratio:850/629;width:100%;\" src=\"https://images.openai.com/static-rsc-4/WZ-UGczTDJ1UBunqd-hqHYYRfU6V2eA9joOYTkk3feMkydM7-_c_wTKH-LynFxSbsmjAyc4JtQghW2Nmr50x4ulWhX6zCYnVCyLLr6lr1962fMu7bPi_3m6PJfx9nvt8HFSixA9p4o-7GJDNKEyBLlqEL5n0lEiaEUJXPJD2bTfJrQThvG7Ej9EcX9xWM9Ev?purpose=fullsize\" alt=\"Increase many trains to Quy Nhon, Da Nang during the New Year holiday 2021.\" width=\"850\" height=\"629\"></li></ul><p>This is particularly suitable for European travelers – who often:</p><ul><li>Stay for extended periods</li><li>Combine multiple destinations in one trip.</li></ul><p>Meanwhile, <strong>Phu Quoc is an isolated destination:</strong></p><ul><li>Completely dependent on flight routes.</li><li>Limited flexibility if schedules change.</li><li>Inter-island travel can sometimes be time-consuming due to long distances.<br><img class=\"image_resized\" style=\"aspect-ratio:700/438;width:100%;\" src=\"https://nld.mediacdn.vn/zoom/700_438/291774122806476800/2025/6/10/phoi-canh-san-bay-phu-quoc-trong-tuong-lai-17495631189951701713454-0-0-1134-1814-crop-1749563242452251115041.jpg\" alt=\"Urgently build Phu Quoc airport to welcome 10 million guests/year.\" width=\"700\" height=\"438\"></li></ul><p>👉 In other words:<br><strong>Phu Quoc is a destination, while Vũng Tàu is part of a journey.</strong><br>&nbsp;</p><h2>Value Received: Not Just Accommodation Costs</h2><p>With the same budget:</p><ul><li>Phu Quoc focuses on experiences within the resort.</li><li>Vũng Tàu offers more options both inside and outside the hotel.</li></ul><p>This creates a difference in \'value\':</p><ul><li>Not just beautiful rooms,</li><li>but the overall experience throughout the vacation.</li></ul><h2>Conclusion: The choice depends on how you wish to enjoy.</h2><p>Phu Quoc is the right choice if you seek:</p><ul><li>Privacy</li><li>Simple relaxation</li><li>Minimal travel.</li></ul><p>Meanwhile, Vũng Tàu is more suitable if you want to:</p><ul><li>Combine relaxation and exploration.</li><li>Experience rich local culture.</li><li>Flexibility in your itinerary.</li></ul><p>For many international travelers – especially from Russia and Europe – who value experiences and diversity,</p><p><strong>Vũng Tàu often provides a more complete vacation, not just on the beach but throughout the entire journey.</strong></p><p>And to fully enjoy the beauty of this coastal city, choosing a sea-view hotel – where you can greet the sunrise over the bay each morning – will be the most refined touch to complete your experience, and Ruby 68 is the perfect choice for you.<br><img src=\"https://scontent.fcxr1-1.fna.fbcdn.net/v/t39.30808-6/528758613_1381815780617190_5952086096816416863_n.jpg?_nc_cat=109&amp;ccb=1-7&amp;_nc_sid=13d280&amp;_nc_ohc=WKHbe34Vi6YQ7kNvwGUvaeL&amp;_nc_oc=AdpGnjU65070UBPhyXNyQfzMjC12wDhv7L0_GZMjcEDoVQzqqXZgNj74U9uPGetQiO4&amp;_nc_zt=23&amp;_nc_ht=scontent.fcxr1-1.fna&amp;_nc_gid=9K_xlEDhU1xGWrSDQFfphg&amp;_nc_ss=7b2a8&amp;oh=00_Af6wgzhT8VBoxuQGiviuD3BXM5CWZTIjbYNTgrpjgNcugA&amp;oe=69FB3E77\" alt=\"May be an image of twilight, pool and horizon.\" width=\"2048\" height=\"1365\"></p></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div>', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1566073771259-6a8506099945?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&h=927&q=80'),
('en_US', 64, 'Is Vũng Tàu Friendly to International Guests? The Latest Travel Experience 2026', 'Is Vũng Tàu friendly to international guests? Discover why this coastal city is increasingly loved by global travelers with its beautiful beaches, 3-star services, reasonable costs, and easy, comfortable resort experiences.', '<h1>Vũng Tàu – A destination that makes international travelers want to return</h1><p>Vũng Tàu is not just a beautiful coastal city.<br>This is a place where <strong>international travelers come once… and want to return many times.</strong></p><p>Why?</p><h2>Arriving in Vũng Tàu – a pleasant feeling from the very first day</h2><p>As soon as you land at Long Thành International Airport, you will realize one thing:</p><p>Everything here <strong>is very easy</strong></p><figure class=\"image\"><img style=\"aspect-ratio:1536/1024;\" src=\"/storage/image-1.png\" alt=\"image-1.png\" width=\"1536\" height=\"1024\"></figure><ul><li>Convenient transportation</li></ul><figure class=\"image image_resized\" style=\"width:98.93%;\"><img style=\"aspect-ratio:730/457;\" src=\"https://cdn2.tuoitre.vn/thumb_w/730/471584752817336320/2025/4/16/1-1744800081772817830225.jpg\" alt=\"Vũng Tàu - Photo 1.\" width=\"730\" height=\"457\"></figure><ul><li>Hotels familiar to international guests</li></ul><figure class=\"image\"><img style=\"aspect-ratio:1500/1000;\" src=\"https://truonghotel.com.vn/assets/uploads/editor/nha%20trang%20-%20dan.jpg\" alt=\"Unforgettable impressions when visiting Vũng Tàu even just once\" width=\"1500\" height=\"1000\"></figure><ul><li>Friendly, open, gentle, and hospitable people</li></ul><p>You don’t need to “learn how to travel” here.<br>You just need to come… and enjoy.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><h2>Beautiful beaches – but not too crowded</h2><p>Vũng Tàu boasts one of the most beautiful bays in Vietnam:</p><figure class=\"image\"><img style=\"aspect-ratio:1080/720;\" src=\"https://movenpickresortcamranh.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/05/1080-%C3%97-720px-2.png\" alt=\"Vũng Tàu Beach for the 2026 Beach Tourism Season\" width=\"1080\" height=\"720\"></figure><ul><li>Clear, calm waters</li><li>Fine, soft sand</li><li>Warm sunshine almost year-round</li></ul><p>Unlike many other famous tourist destinations, Vũng Tàu offers a feeling of <strong>comfort, not too stuffy, not too crowded</strong>.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><h2>3-star experiences at reasonable costs</h2><p>This is why many international travelers are surprised, as Vũng Tàu has a plethora of hotels across various segments for easy selection</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>At hotels like Ruby 68 Hotel, the experience is elevated to international standards with personalized service, providing a true relaxation retreat.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><h2>A city familiar to international guests</h2><p>Vũng Tàu is not a “new” destination.</p><figure class=\"image\"><img style=\"aspect-ratio:1440/960;\" src=\"https://baokhanhhoa.vn/file/e7837c02857c8ca30185a8c39b582c03/082024/338533142_954584469209734_8893263659800164664_n_20240823161240.jpg\" alt=\"International guests to Ba Ria - Vung Tau have exceeded the 2024 plan\" width=\"1440\" height=\"960\"></figure><p>This is a place loved by:</p><ul><li>Russian &amp; CIS guests</li><li>Korean and Japanese guests</li><li>European guests (France, Germany, Netherlands, Poland…)</li><li>Australian - American guests</li></ul><p>This means:<br>👉 This city is accustomed to serving international guests</p><p>&nbsp;</p><h2>Easy travel – no pressure</h2><p>You can:</p><ul><li>Quickly book online</li><li>Use services in English or many other languages</li><li>Easily find suitable tours, restaurants, and experiences</li></ul><p>Not complicated. No barriers.</p><h2>Not just a trip – but a feeling</h2><p>Vũng Tàu is not a place to “check off a list.”</p><figure class=\"image\"><img style=\"aspect-ratio:2560/1920;\" src=\"https://baokhanhhoa.vn/file/e7837c02857c8ca30185a8c39b582c03/062024/bien_-_nhan_tam_20240624145335_20240624164935.jpg\" alt=\"The city stretches to welcome the sunrise - Ba Ria - Vung Tau Electronic Newspaper\" width=\"2560\" height=\"1920\"></figure><p>But a place to:</p><ul><li>Watch the sunrise over the sea</li><li>Relax by the pool</li><li>Enjoy body care services</li><li>And truly unwind</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><h2>So is Vũng Tàu friendly to international guests?</h2><p>👉 Not just friendly.<br>👉 But also <strong>easy to visit – easy to stay – easy to love</strong></p><p>If you are looking for a place:</p><ul><li>Beautiful beaches</li><li>Good service</li><li>Reasonable costs</li><li>Not too crowded</li></ul><p><strong>Vũng Tàu is a choice well worth experiencing.</strong></p>', NULL);
INSERT INTO `posts_translations` (`lang_code`, `posts_id`, `name`, `description`, `content`, `image`) VALUES
('en_US', 65, 'Long Thành Beach Travel Guide', 'Long Thành (Bà Rịa - Vũng Tàu) is renowned for Bai Dai – one of the top 10 most beautiful beaches in the world. This area boasts a high-end resort ecosystem with dozens of international resorts, 300 sunny days each year, making it ideal for travel from February to August. In addition to swimming and team-building activities, visitors can explore the Gạc Ma Memorial, the Snail Pagoda, the Tidal Lag', '<div class=\"section-inner inset-column\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial, serif;font-size:20px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;margin:0px auto;max-width:710px;padding:0px 15px;text-align:left;width:710px;word-spacing:0px;\"><p style=\"font-family:Arial;line-height:32px;margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;\">Long Thành Beach is located in Cam Lâm district, <a style=\"color:rgb(22,143,214);margin:0px;padding:0px;\" href=\"https://vnexpress.net/cam-nang-du-lich-ba-ria-vung-tau-4759133.html\"><u>Bà Rịa - Vũng Tàu</u></a>. The highlight of Long Thành is Bai Dai, which features a 16 km long crescent-shaped coastline, close to the airport.</p><p style=\"font-family:Arial;line-height:32px;margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;\">The sea is crystal clear, with white sandy beaches and gentle waves, perfect for relaxation and recreational activities by the sea. Here, a tourism ecosystem has formed, offering a full range of services and numerous experiences.</p></div><p><img class=\"image_resized\" style=\"aspect-ratio:2400/1599;font-size:0px;line-height:0;margin:0px;max-width:100%;padding:0px;width:1100px;\" src=\"https://i1-dulich.vnecdn.net/2026/05/08/Bai-Dai-1778233919-3120-1778258994.webp?w=0&amp;h=0&amp;q=100&amp;dpr=1&amp;fit=crop&amp;s=nJB2vfNnoqsuDNjNceyH0Q\" alt=\"\" width=\"2400\" height=\"1599\"></p><div class=\"section-inner outset-column\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial, serif;font-size:20px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;margin:0px auto;max-width:1130px;padding:0px 15px;text-align:left;width:1130px;word-spacing:0px;\"><div class=\"medium-insert-images medium-insert-images-large\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;text-align:center;\"><figure style=\"margin:0px;max-width:100%;padding:0px;\"><figcaption style=\"color:rgb(79,79,79);font-family:arial;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;line-height:27.2px;margin:0px auto;max-width:670px;padding:10px 0px 0px;text-align:left;\">A corner of Bai Dai Long Thành. Photo: <i style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;\">Bà Rịa - Vũng Tàu Tourism Promotion Center</i></figcaption></figure></div></div><div class=\"section-inner inset-column\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial, serif;font-size:20px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;margin:0px auto;max-width:710px;padding:0px 15px;text-align:left;width:710px;word-spacing:0px;\"><p style=\"font-family:Arial;line-height:32px;margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;\">Long Thành has appeared on the world tourism map with Bai Dai being selected by <em style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><i>National Geographic</i></em> as one of the 10 most beautiful beaches in the world, and Long Thành Bay is considered one of the most beautiful natural bays globally, alongside San Francisco (USA) and Rio De Janeiro (Brazil)... In 2018, the magazine <em style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><i>CnTraveler </i></em>suggested readers take a vacation in Long Thành due to its beautiful beaches with 300 sunny days each year. The dating show <em style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><i>The Bachelor</i></em> from <em style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><i>ABC </i></em>(USA) chose a resort in Long Thành as its backdrop.</p><p style=\"font-family:Arial;line-height:32px;margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;\">Visitors should come to Long Thành from February to August when the weather is sunny and the sea is calm. The last months of the year are the rainy season in Long Thành, but the rain usually only falls in the late afternoon and rarely lasts continuously.</p></div><div class=\"section-inner inset-column\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial, serif;font-size:20px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;margin:0px auto;max-width:710px;padding:0px 15px;text-align:left;width:710px;word-spacing:0px;\"><h3 class=\"d5d0d81a3e87bf8b3395\" style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial, sans-serif;font-size:26px;line-height:1.313;margin:0px 0px 1.05263rem;min-height:1px;padding:0px;text-align:center;\"><strong>Transportation</strong></h3><p style=\"font-family:Arial;line-height:32px;margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;\">Long Thành is located in the southern part of Bà Rịa - Vũng Tàu province, about 30 km from the center of <a style=\"color:rgb(22,143,214);margin:0px;padding:0px;\" href=\"https://vnexpress.net/cam-nang-du-lich-vung-tau-tu-a-den-z-4127199.html\"><u>Vũng Tàu</u></a> , conveniently connected by transportation.</p><p style=\"font-family:Arial;line-height:32px;margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;\"><b style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>Getting to Long Thành</strong></b></p><p style=\"font-family:Arial;line-height:32px;margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;\"><i style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;\">By Road</i></p><p style=\"font-family:Arial;line-height:32px;margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;\">Visitors can reach Long Thành by road via National Route 1A or the North-South Expressway (CT01). In 2024, once the Ho Chi Minh City - Cam Lâm expressway is completed, travel time from Ho Chi Minh City will be about 6-8 hours, while from the center of Vũng Tàu, it will take about 45-60 minutes, depending on traffic conditions. Common transportation options include sleeper buses, private cars, or motorbikes.</p></div><p><img style=\"font-size:0px;line-height:0;margin:0px;max-width:100%;padding:0px;\" src=\"https://i1-dulich.vnecdn.net/2026/05/08/sbcm-1778235858-3130-1778258994.webp?w=0&amp;h=0&amp;q=100&amp;dpr=1&amp;fit=crop&amp;s=U0K6KCgAKrXxn2YhxmNwPQ\" alt=\"\" width=\"1360\" height=\"842\"></p><div class=\"section-inner inset-column\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial, serif;font-size:20px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;margin:0px auto;max-width:710px;padding:0px 15px;text-align:left;width:710px;word-spacing:0px;\"><div class=\"medium-insert-images\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;text-align:center;\"><figure style=\"margin:0px;max-width:100%;padding:0px;\"><figcaption style=\"color:rgb(79,79,79);font-family:arial;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;line-height:27.2px;margin:0px auto;max-width:670px;padding:10px 0px 0px;text-align:left;\">A panoramic view of Long Thành Airport. Photo: <em style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><i>ACV</i></em></figcaption></figure></div><p style=\"font-family:Arial;line-height:32px;margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;\"><i style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;\">By Air</i></p><p style=\"font-family:Arial;line-height:32px;margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;\">Long Thành Airport is located on Long Thành Beach. This is an international airport, the main aviation hub of the region, welcoming direct flights from cities such as Seoul and Busan (South Korea), Kuala Lumpur (Malaysia), Almaty (Kazakhstan), and Bangkok (Thailand), along with daily domestic flights from Vietjet Air, Vietnam Airlines, and Bamboo Airways from Ho Chi Minh City, Hanoi, Da Nang...</p><p style=\"font-family:Arial;line-height:32px;margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;\">Travel time from the airport to the resorts ranges from 5 to 20 minutes, depending on location. Visitors can hire taxis outside the airport (5-7 seat type) or use Vinbus and Dat Moi buses on the Long Thành - Vũng Tàu route, which stop at several points along Bai Dai.</p><p style=\"font-family:Arial;line-height:32px;margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;\"><i style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;\">By Train</i></p><p style=\"font-family:Arial;line-height:32px;margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;\">The Thống Nhất trains departing from Hanoi or Ho Chi Minh City all stop at Vũng Tàu station. Visitors can travel to Long Thành by bus or taxi.</p><p style=\"font-family:Arial;line-height:32px;margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;\"><b style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>Getting Around Long Thành</strong></b></p></div><p><img style=\"font-size:0px;line-height:0;margin:0px;max-width:100%;padding:0px;\" src=\"https://i1-dulich.vnecdn.net/2026/05/08/CM-1778235671-7263-1778258994.png?w=0&amp;h=0&amp;q=100&amp;dpr=1&amp;fit=crop&amp;s=ycHIEIjKKlPchsh_6Z2tFw\" alt=\"\" width=\"1100\" height=\"619\"></p><div class=\"section-inner inset-column\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial, serif;font-size:20px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;margin:0px auto;max-width:710px;padding:0px 15px;text-align:left;width:710px;word-spacing:0px;\"><div class=\"medium-insert-images\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;text-align:center;\"><figure style=\"margin:0px;max-width:100%;padding:0px;\"><figcaption style=\"color:rgb(79,79,79);font-family:arial;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;line-height:27.2px;margin:0px auto;max-width:670px;padding:10px 0px 0px;text-align:left;\">Nguyễn Tất Thành, the main road in Long Thành. Photo: <i style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;\">Cafeland</i></figcaption></figure></div><p style=\"font-family:Arial;line-height:32px;margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;\">Nguyễn Tất Thành is the main road in Long Thành, also known as DT6571, connecting from the Long Thành Airport area to the center of Vũng Tàu.</p><p style=\"font-family:Arial;line-height:32px;margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;\">In Long Thành, visitors can rent motorbikes for prices ranging from 120,000 VND to 200,000 VND per day, depending on whether it is a scooter or a manual bike.</p><p style=\"font-family:Arial;line-height:32px;margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;\">Visitors can also rent bicycles for prices ranging from 50,000 VND to 120,000 VND. Rental periods are flexible, by the hour, day, or month. Bicycles come in various types.</p><p style=\"font-family:Arial;line-height:32px;margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;\">Shuttle buses from each hotel or resort will also transport guests to certain attractions in Long Thành or Vũng Tàu. Guests should contact in advance for more details.</p></div><div class=\"section-inner inset-column\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial, serif;font-size:20px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;margin:0px auto;max-width:710px;padding:0px 15px;text-align:left;width:710px;word-spacing:0px;\"><h3 class=\"32e5d8f585fdba5aa1e4\" style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial, sans-serif;font-size:26px;line-height:1.313;margin:0px 0px 1.05263rem;min-height:1px;padding:0px;text-align:center;\"><strong>Accommodation</strong></h3><p style=\"font-family:Arial;line-height:32px;margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;\">Over the past decade, the number of hotels and resorts at Long Thành beach has rapidly increased. There are currently dozens of resorts, hotels, and homestays operating in the area, offering a variety of accommodation options, including many world-renowned brands.</p><p style=\"font-family:Arial;line-height:32px;margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;\"><b style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>Luxury Resorts</strong></b></p><p style=\"font-family:Arial;line-height:32px;margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;\">Top global hotel brands such as JW Marriott, Movenpick, Wyndham, Ana Mandara, <span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);\"><span style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;\">Radisson Blu, Westin, Fusion, Melia... as well as other famous brands like The Anam, Alma, Riveria, Selectum Noa, Duyên Hà... all have luxury resorts on Long Thành beach.</span> &nbsp;</span></p><p style=\"font-family:Arial;line-height:32px;margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;\"><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);\"><span style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;\">The resorts are all located along Bai Dai, featuring private beaches, various room categories, and high-end services such as swimming pools, spas, conference areas, entertainment centers, sports facilities, and children\'s clubs. Prices start from 3 million VND per night.</span> &nbsp;</span></p></div><p><img class=\"image_resized\" style=\"aspect-ratio:2048/1365;font-size:0px;line-height:0;margin:0px;max-width:100%;padding:0px;width:1100px;\" src=\"https://i1-dulich.vnecdn.net/2026/05/08/Ma1-1778231885-6817-1778258994.jpg?w=0&amp;h=0&amp;q=100&amp;dpr=1&amp;fit=crop&amp;s=OT_It36DnoCB_necvqBteg\" alt=\"\" width=\"2048\" height=\"1365\"></p><div class=\"section-inner outset-column\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial, serif;font-size:20px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;margin:0px auto;max-width:1130px;padding:0px 15px;text-align:left;width:1130px;word-spacing:0px;\"><div class=\"section-inner outset-column\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial, serif;font-size:20px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;margin:0px auto;max-width:1130px;padding:0px 15px;text-align:left;width:1130px;word-spacing:0px;\"><div class=\"medium-insert-images medium-insert-images-large\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;text-align:center;\"><figure style=\"margin:0px;max-width:100%;padding:0px;\"><figcaption style=\"color:rgb(79,79,79);font-family:arial;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;line-height:27.2px;margin:0px auto;max-width:670px;padding:10px 0px 0px;text-align:left;\">JW Marriott Long Thành is one of the newest and most luxurious resorts in Long Thành. Photo: <i style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;\">Resorts</i></figcaption></figure></div></div></div><div class=\"section-inner inset-column\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial, serif;font-size:20px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;margin:0px auto;max-width:710px;padding:0px 15px;text-align:left;width:710px;word-spacing:0px;\"><p style=\"font-family:Arial;line-height:32px;margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;\"><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);\"><b style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><span style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>Hotels and Homestays</strong></span><strong> &nbsp;</strong></b></span></p><p style=\"font-family:Arial;line-height:32px;margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;\"><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);\"><span style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;\">In addition to high-end resorts along the coast, the Long Thành area also has many hotels and homestays located in North Long Thành, Cam Nghĩa, along Hùng Vương Road (National Route 1A), about 5 km from Bai Dai, towards Cầu Mới or the Long Thành welcome gate.</span> &nbsp;</span></p><p style=\"font-family:Arial;line-height:32px;margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;\"><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);\"><span style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;\">Some recommended 2-3 star hotels include Sơn Hiển Hotel, Lan Anh Hotel, Magnolia Long Thành, Triều Khang Hotel, Mỹ Ca, Navy Hotel, Santorini Villa... Room rates range from 300,000 VND per night.</span> &nbsp;</span></p></div><div class=\"section-inner inset-column\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial, serif;font-size:20px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;margin:0px auto;max-width:710px;padding:0px 15px;text-align:left;width:710px;word-spacing:0px;\"><h3 class=\"4fc8d92ea5f1bb48554e\" style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial, sans-serif;font-size:26px;line-height:1.313;margin:0px 0px 1.05263rem;min-height:1px;padding:0px;text-align:center;\"><strong>Cuisine</strong></h3><p style=\"font-family:Arial;line-height:32px;margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;\"><b style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>Fresh Seafood</strong></b></p><p style=\"font-family:Arial;line-height:32px;margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;\">The Tidal Lagoon area and the streets near Cầu Mới, at the end of Nguyễn Tất Thành Road (about 10 km from Long Thành Airport), are home to many restaurants and eateries offering a variety of options. Visitors can choose from places like Bờ Kè Seafood, Bến Thuyền Seafood, Hải Yến Seafood, Hương Biển Restaurant, Hải sản Mộng Ước, Hải sản Em Ơi... Fresh dishes of the day are available, with comfortable and cool seating. Costs per person start from 200,000 VND.</p><p style=\"font-family:Arial;line-height:32px;margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;\">Long Thành is famous for its lobsters, blood clams, oysters, various types of snails, abalone, and mackerel...</p></div><p><img style=\"font-size:0px;line-height:0;margin:0px;max-width:100%;padding:0px;\" src=\"https://i1-dulich.vnecdn.net/2026/05/08/z7804480523936-fd88101735aed0d-4189-7685-1778258995.jpg?w=0&amp;h=0&amp;q=100&amp;dpr=1&amp;fit=crop&amp;s=dgs8523JOs1w49xVocOmWw\" alt=\"\" width=\"1280\" height=\"960\"></p><div class=\"section-inner inset-column\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial, serif;font-size:20px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;margin:0px auto;max-width:710px;padding:0px 15px;text-align:left;width:710px;word-spacing:0px;\"><div class=\"medium-insert-images\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;text-align:center;\"><figure style=\"margin:0px;max-width:100%;padding:0px;\"><figcaption style=\"color:rgb(79,79,79);font-family:arial;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;line-height:27.2px;margin:0px auto;max-width:670px;padding:10px 0px 0px;text-align:left;\">Seafood restaurant on the Tidal Lagoon, near Cầu Mới. Photo: <i style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;\">Linh Hương</i></figcaption></figure></div><p style=\"font-family:Arial;line-height:32px;margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;\"><b style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>Local Specialties</strong></b></p><p style=\"font-family:Arial;line-height:32px;margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;\">In addition to seafood, visitors to Long Thành should not miss local specialties such as bánh xèo, grilled spring rolls, chicken, and bánh căn...</p><p style=\"font-family:Arial;line-height:32px;margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;\"><i style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;\">Bánh căn</i></p></div><p><img style=\"font-size:0px;line-height:0;margin:0px;max-width:100%;padding:0px;\" src=\"https://i1-dulich.vnecdn.net/2026/05/08/banh-can1-1778238245-9851-1778258995.webp?w=0&amp;h=0&amp;q=100&amp;dpr=1&amp;fit=crop&amp;s=knAJRRaKffaaPeZnTGJxRg\" alt=\"\" width=\"2400\" height=\"1800\"></p><div class=\"section-inner inset-column\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial, serif;font-size:20px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;margin:0px auto;max-width:710px;padding:0px 15px;text-align:left;width:710px;word-spacing:0px;\"><div class=\"medium-insert-images\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;text-align:center;\"><figure style=\"margin:0px;max-width:100%;padding:0px;\"><figcaption style=\"color:rgb(79,79,79);font-family:arial;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;line-height:27.2px;margin:0px auto;max-width:670px;padding:10px 0px 0px;text-align:left;\">Bánh căn is a specialty of Bà Rịa - Vũng Tàu. Photo: <i style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;\">Đông Phong</i></figcaption></figure></div><p style=\"font-family:Arial;line-height:32px;margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"font-family:Arial;line-height:32px;margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;\">Bánh căn is baked in clay molds. The cakes are small, round, with a lightly crispy outer layer but soft and fluffy inside. The filling is diverse, including quail eggs, chicken eggs, shrimp, fresh squid, or minced meat. When baking, pork fat is brushed on the mold to create a fragrant aroma. The cakes are served with sweet and sour fish sauce or fermented fish sauce.</p><p style=\"font-family:Arial;line-height:32px;margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;\">&gt;&gt; See more: <a style=\"color:rgb(22,143,214);margin:0px;padding:0px;\" href=\"https://vnexpress.net/banh-can-2-000-dong-o-vung-tau-4666498.html\"><b style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong><u>Bánh căn 2,000 VND in Vũng Tàu</u></strong></b></a></p><p style=\"font-family:Arial;line-height:32px;margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;\"><i style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;\">Ninh Hòa Grilled Spring Rolls</i></p><p style=\"font-family:Arial;line-height:32px;margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;\">Ninh Hòa Grilled Spring Rolls are also a local specialty. Lean pork thigh is finely ground, mixed with shredded pig skin, seasoned well, then shaped into long rolls, skewered and grilled over hot coals until crispy. When eating, diners wrap the spring rolls with fresh herbs, crispy rice paper, green mango, cucumber, and sour banana. The dipping sauce is made from glutinous rice, soybeans, tomatoes, shrimp, and pig liver, blended until thick.</p><p style=\"font-family:Arial;line-height:32px;margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;\"><i style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;\">Bánh xèo</i></p></div><p><img style=\"font-size:0px;line-height:0;margin:0px;max-width:100%;padding:0px;\" src=\"https://i1-dulich.vnecdn.net/2026/05/08/banhxeo-1778238337-5309-1778258995.webp?w=0&amp;h=0&amp;q=100&amp;dpr=1&amp;fit=crop&amp;s=TQG-Smv3C5pv2v9-lLsEug\" alt=\"\" width=\"1020\" height=\"680\"></p><div class=\"section-inner inset-column\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial, serif;font-size:20px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;margin:0px auto;max-width:710px;padding:0px 15px;text-align:left;width:710px;word-spacing:0px;\"><div class=\"medium-insert-images\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;text-align:center;\"><figure style=\"margin:0px;max-width:100%;padding:0px;\"><figcaption style=\"color:rgb(79,79,79);font-family:arial;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;line-height:27.2px;margin:0px auto;max-width:670px;padding:10px 0px 0px;text-align:left;\">Squid bánh xèo. Photo: <i style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;\">Bùi Toàn</i></figcaption></figure></div><p style=\"font-family:Arial;line-height:32px;margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;\">Bánh xèo is usually small, about the size of a hand, with a thin, golden, and crispy crust. The filling typically includes small whole fresh squid, shrimp, pork belly, and bean sprouts. The dish\'s flavor combines the crispiness of the batter, the natural sweetness of fresh seafood, and the richness of pork fat. The dish is served with diluted fish sauce, sweet and sour, sometimes with fish sauce.</p><p style=\"font-family:Arial;line-height:32px;margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;\">&gt;&gt; See more: <a style=\"color:rgb(22,143,214);margin:0px;padding:0px;\" href=\"https://vnexpress.net/quan-banh-xeo-muc-70-nam-o-vung-tau-4562428.html\"><b style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong><u>70-year-old squid bánh xèo restaurant in Vũng Tàu</u></strong></b></a></p><p style=\"font-family:Arial;line-height:32px;margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;\">In addition to the mentioned dishes, Long Thành also offers specialties like mango, durian, mangosteen, and many other tropical fruits.</p></div><div class=\"section-inner inset-column\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial, serif;font-size:20px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;margin:0px auto;max-width:710px;padding:0px 15px;text-align:left;width:710px;word-spacing:0px;\"><h3 class=\"ef2ea7a895ee551ef4e9\" style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial, sans-serif;font-size:26px;line-height:1.313;margin:0px 0px 1.05263rem;min-height:1px;padding:0px;text-align:center;\"><strong>Entertainment - Sightseeing</strong></h3><p style=\"font-family:Arial;line-height:32px;margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;\"><b style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>Beach Activities</strong></b></p></div><p><img style=\"font-size:0px;line-height:0;margin:0px;max-width:100%;padding:0px;\" src=\"https://i1-dulich.vnecdn.net/2026/05/08/Sea-1778234471-4589-1778258995.jpg?w=0&amp;h=0&amp;q=100&amp;dpr=1&amp;fit=crop&amp;s=_aDSRbz5r0AboGS1bz0YqA\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"675\"></p><div class=\"section-inner inset-column\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial, serif;font-size:20px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;margin:0px auto;max-width:710px;padding:0px 15px;text-align:left;width:710px;word-spacing:0px;\"><div class=\"medium-insert-images\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;text-align:center;\"><figure style=\"margin:0px;max-width:100%;padding:0px;\"><figcaption style=\"color:rgb(79,79,79);font-family:arial;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;line-height:27.2px;margin:0px auto;max-width:670px;padding:10px 0px 0px;text-align:left;\">The area for beach games in Long Thành by Sealife. Photo: <i style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;\">Sealife</i></figcaption></figure></div><p style=\"font-family:Arial;line-height:32px;margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;\">Beach activities in Long Thành are diverse, including thrilling activities like jet skiing, parasailing, banana boating, and surfing, as well as gentler activities like paddleboarding, kayaking, snorkeling, and team-building activities such as tug-of-war and beach volleyball.</p><p style=\"font-family:Arial;line-height:32px;margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;\">Activities usually take place early in the morning or in the afternoon along Bai Dai. Visitors can refer to organizing units like Sealife, Surfbase, or contact the resorts in advance.</p><p style=\"font-family:Arial;line-height:32px;margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;\"><b style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>Gạc Ma Soldier Memorial</strong></b></p></div><p><img class=\"image_resized\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1280/960;font-size:0px;line-height:0;margin:0px;max-width:100%;padding:0px;width:1100px;\" src=\"https://i1-dulich.vnecdn.net/2026/05/08/GM2-1778233250-6720-1778258995.jpg?w=0&amp;h=0&amp;q=100&amp;dpr=1&amp;fit=crop&amp;s=wKDg3DR4_81LSYrr_n-Ihw\" alt=\"\" width=\"1280\" height=\"960\"></p><div class=\"section-inner outset-column\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial, serif;font-size:20px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;margin:0px auto;max-width:1130px;padding:0px 15px;text-align:left;width:1130px;word-spacing:0px;\"><div class=\"medium-insert-images medium-insert-images-large\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;text-align:center;\"><figure style=\"margin:0px;max-width:100%;padding:0px;\"><figcaption style=\"color:rgb(79,79,79);font-family:arial;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;line-height:27.2px;margin:0px auto;max-width:670px;padding:10px 0px 0px;text-align:left;\">The monument at the Gạc Ma Soldier Memorial. Photo: <i style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;\">Linh Hương</i></figcaption></figure></div></div><div class=\"section-inner inset-column\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial, serif;font-size:20px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;margin:0px auto;max-width:710px;padding:0px 15px;text-align:left;width:710px;word-spacing:0px;\"><p style=\"font-family:Arial;line-height:32px;margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;\">The memorial was built on an area of 25,000 m2, with an investment of 130 billion VND, completing phase one in 2017. It features a museum of 220 m2, highlighted by an exhibition area displaying photographs and artifacts of 64 soldiers who sacrificed their lives in the battle to defend Gạc Ma, part of the Spratly Islands (Bà Rịa - Vũng Tàu), along with documents (including letters and ancient maps, images...) about the process of exploration, establishing, and enforcing Vietnam\'s sovereignty over the Paracel and Spratly Islands.</p><p style=\"font-family:Arial;line-height:32px;margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;\">In addition to the museum, the memorial also includes a monument cluster and landscaped areas...</p></div><div class=\"section-inner outset-column\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial, serif;font-size:20px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;margin:0px auto;max-width:1130px;padding:0px 15px;text-align:left;width:1130px;word-spacing:0px;\"><div class=\"medium-insert-embeds medium-insert-embeds-gallery medium-insert-embeds-normal medium-insert-embeds-large\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;text-align:center;\"><figure style=\"margin:0px auto 20px;max-width:100%;padding:0px;\"><div class=\"medium-insert-embed\" style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><div class=\"width_common gallery_block gallery_processed\" style=\"color:rgb(79,79,79);font:400 16px/22.4px arial;margin:0px 0px 20px;padding:0px;width:1100px;\"><div class=\"inner_gallery_new\" style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;\" id=\"gallery_new_3\"><div class=\"item_gallery_new\" style=\"margin:0px 20px 0px 0px;padding:0px;\"><figure class=\"image\"><a href=\"https://i1-dulich.vnecdn.net/2026/05/08/GM1-1778233291-8343-1778258995.jpg?w=0&amp;h=0&amp;q=100&amp;dpr=1&amp;fit=crop&amp;s=pYaiubIKJWpYVFgVMSvvgQ\"><img style=\"aspect-ratio:364/273;font-size:0px;line-height:0;margin:0px;max-width:100%;padding:0px;\" src=\"https://i1-dulich.vnecdn.net/2026/05/08/GM1-1778233291-8343-1778258995.jpg?w=0&amp;h=0&amp;q=100&amp;dpr=1&amp;fit=crop&amp;s=pYaiubIKJWpYVFgVMSvvgQ\" alt=\"GM1-1778233291.jpg\" width=\"364\" height=\"273\"></a></figure><div class=\"desc_cation\" style=\"margin:0px auto;max-width:680px;padding:15px 0px 0px;text-align:left;\">The memorial space for Gạc Ma soldiers. Photo: Linh Hương</div></div><div class=\"item_gallery_new\" style=\"margin:0px 20px 0px 0px;padding:0px;\"><figure class=\"image\"><a href=\"https://i1-dulich.vnecdn.net/2026/05/08/GM3-1778233291-9797-1778258995.jpg?w=0&amp;h=0&amp;q=100&amp;dpr=1&amp;fit=crop&amp;s=q-Q78t-2N2X6OtsIY9wSwQ\"><img style=\"aspect-ratio:364/273;font-size:0px;line-height:0;margin:0px;max-width:100%;padding:0px;\" src=\"https://i1-dulich.vnecdn.net/2026/05/08/GM3-1778233291-9797-1778258995.jpg?w=0&amp;h=0&amp;q=100&amp;dpr=1&amp;fit=crop&amp;s=q-Q78t-2N2X6OtsIY9wSwQ\" alt=\"GM3-1778233291.jpg\" width=\"364\" height=\"273\"></a></figure><div class=\"desc_cation\" style=\"margin:0px auto;max-width:680px;padding:15px 0px 0px;text-align:left;\">Inside the Gạc Ma Museum. Photo: Linh Hương</div></div><div class=\"item_gallery_new\" style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><figure class=\"image\"><a href=\"https://i1-dulich.vnecdn.net/2026/05/08/GM4-1778233291-6832-1778258995.jpg?w=0&amp;h=0&amp;q=100&amp;dpr=1&amp;fit=crop&amp;s=W69oiCV_vyASkvCgKyZR-Q\"><img style=\"aspect-ratio:364/273;font-size:0px;line-height:0;margin:0px;max-width:100%;padding:0px;\" src=\"https://i1-dulich.vnecdn.net/2026/05/08/GM4-1778233291-6832-1778258995.jpg?w=0&amp;h=0&amp;q=100&amp;dpr=1&amp;fit=crop&amp;s=W69oiCV_vyASkvCgKyZR-Q\" alt=\"GM4-1778233291.jpg\" width=\"364\" height=\"273\"></a></figure><div class=\"desc_cation\" style=\"margin:0px auto;max-width:680px;padding:15px 0px 0px;text-align:left;\">Artifacts. Photo: Linh Hương</div></div></div></div></div></figure></div></div><div class=\"section-inner inset-column\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial, serif;font-size:20px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;margin:0px auto;max-width:710px;padding:0px 15px;text-align:left;width:710px;word-spacing:0px;\"><p style=\"font-family:Arial;line-height:32px;margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;\"><b style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>Axi Plaza Shopping Center</strong></b></p><p style=\"font-family:Arial;line-height:32px;margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;\">Opened in April 2024, located in the center of Bai Dai, Axi Plaza integrates many amenities. The large hall and banquet room on the 3rd floor cover 1,200 m2 and can accommodate 1,000 people. The 360-degree rooftop on the 5th floor is reserved for banquets and events. The indoor and outdoor dining area is on the 4th floor. The 1st floor is for shopping with 46 stores. Axi Plaza also features Shop Street, a new entertainment, shopping, and leisure destination, combining a commercial street model with an open seaside space, featuring restaurants, cafes, and various experiential activities.</p></div><p><img style=\"font-size:0px;line-height:0;margin:0px;max-width:100%;padding:0px;\" src=\"https://i1-dulich.vnecdn.net/2026/05/08/477298884-589206017429661-4994-4831-4824-1778258996.jpg?w=0&amp;h=0&amp;q=100&amp;dpr=1&amp;fit=crop&amp;s=simXyG8_C8iXAF9DfTI7gw\" alt=\"\" width=\"2048\" height=\"1073\"></p><div class=\"section-inner inset-column\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial, serif;font-size:20px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;margin:0px auto;max-width:710px;padding:0px 15px;text-align:left;width:710px;word-spacing:0px;\"><div class=\"medium-insert-images\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;text-align:center;\"><figure style=\"margin:0px;max-width:100%;padding:0px;\"><figcaption style=\"color:rgb(79,79,79);font-family:arial;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;line-height:27.2px;margin:0px auto;max-width:670px;padding:10px 0px 0px;text-align:left;\">The outdoor area of Axi Plaza. Photo: <i style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;\">Axi</i></figcaption></figure></div><p style=\"font-family:Arial;line-height:32px;margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;\"><b style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>Tidal Lagoon</strong></b></p><p style=\"font-family:Arial;line-height:32px;margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;\">This is a vast lagoon area, stretching over one-third of the Long Thành peninsula. It offers lush beauty with coastal mangrove forests and a peaceful, leisurely pace of life on the water. Additionally, the natural hot spring is an attractive destination, drawing visitors with health-enhancing services such as mineral soaking, mud baths, herbal baths, and functional recovery, aligning with wellness travel trends.</p><p style=\"font-family:Arial;line-height:32px;margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;\">Visitors seeking relaxation in an ecological space need only take a few steps from Bai Dai to the Tidal Lagoon.</p></div><p><img style=\"font-size:0px;line-height:0;margin:0px;max-width:100%;padding:0px;\" src=\"https://i1-dulich.vnecdn.net/2026/05/08/z7804480496195-bbf0d8cf74700fc-7155-9183-1778258996.jpg?w=0&amp;h=0&amp;q=100&amp;dpr=1&amp;fit=crop&amp;s=UwAhkVgQfBqF9bC1azAwkA\" alt=\"\" width=\"1280\" height=\"960\"></p><div class=\"section-inner inset-column\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial, serif;font-size:20px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;margin:0px auto;max-width:710px;padding:0px 15px;text-align:left;width:710px;word-spacing:0px;\"><div class=\"medium-insert-images\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;text-align:center;\"><figure style=\"margin:0px;max-width:100%;padding:0px;\"><figcaption style=\"color:rgb(79,79,79);font-family:arial;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;line-height:27.2px;margin:0px auto;max-width:670px;padding:10px 0px 0px;text-align:left;\">The New Bridge over the Tidal Lagoon. Photo: <i style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;\">Linh Hương</i></figcaption></figure></div><p style=\"font-family:Arial;line-height:32px;margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;\"><b style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>Từ Vân Snail Pagoda</strong></b></p><p style=\"font-family:Arial;line-height:32px;margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;\">Từ Vân Pagoda is a famous tourist destination that attracts visitors seeking a peaceful atmosphere. The pagoda was built in 1968 and is also known as Coral Pagoda or Snail Pagoda because entering it feels like stepping into an underwater world, with every nook and cranny adorned with shells, clams, and coral stones. The most impressive structure in the pagoda is the Bảo Tích tower, designed and built by the head monk Thích Thông Anh and other monks over five years.</p><p style=\"font-family:Arial;line-height:32px;margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;\"><b style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>Citeaux Mỹ Ca Monastery</strong></b></p></div><div class=\"section-inner outset-column\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial, serif;font-size:20px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;margin:0px auto;max-width:1130px;padding:0px 15px;text-align:left;width:1130px;word-spacing:0px;\"><div class=\"medium-insert-embeds medium-insert-embeds-gallery medium-insert-embeds-normal medium-insert-embeds-large\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;text-align:center;\"><figure style=\"margin:0px auto 20px;max-width:100%;padding:0px;\"><div class=\"medium-insert-embed\" style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><div class=\"width_common gallery_block gallery_processed\" style=\"color:rgb(79,79,79);font:400 16px/22.4px arial;margin:0px 0px 20px;padding:0px;width:1100px;\"><div class=\"inner_gallery_new\" style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;\" id=\"gallery_new_1\"><div class=\"item_gallery_new\" style=\"margin:0px 20px 0px 0px;padding:0px;\"><figure class=\"image\"><a href=\"https://i1-dulich.vnecdn.net/2026/05/08/tuvien1-1778234642-1737-1778258996.jpg?w=0&amp;h=0&amp;q=100&amp;dpr=1&amp;fit=crop&amp;s=BAI67xDMSljkP3MF8Y8iqQ\"><img style=\"aspect-ratio:555/370;font-size:0px;line-height:0;margin:0px;max-width:100%;padding:0px;\" src=\"https://i1-dulich.vnecdn.net/2026/05/08/tuvien1-1778234642-1737-1778258996.jpg?w=0&amp;h=0&amp;q=100&amp;dpr=1&amp;fit=crop&amp;s=BAI67xDMSljkP3MF8Y8iqQ\" alt=\"tuvien1-1778234642.jpg\" width=\"555\" height=\"370\"></a></figure><div class=\"desc_cation\" style=\"margin:0px auto;max-width:680px;padding:15px 0px 0px;text-align:left;\">Ruins of the monastery seen from afar. Photo: Quốc Lê</div></div><div class=\"item_gallery_new\" style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><figure class=\"image\"><a href=\"https://i1-dulich.vnecdn.net/2026/05/08/tuvien2-1778234642-6726-1778258996.jpg?w=0&amp;h=0&amp;q=100&amp;dpr=1&amp;fit=crop&amp;s=8kEepgL0z7HwW2tT8dMu8w\"><img style=\"aspect-ratio:555/370;font-size:0px;line-height:0;margin:0px;max-width:100%;padding:0px;\" src=\"https://i1-dulich.vnecdn.net/2026/05/08/tuvien2-1778234642-6726-1778258996.jpg?w=0&amp;h=0&amp;q=100&amp;dpr=1&amp;fit=crop&amp;s=8kEepgL0z7HwW2tT8dMu8w\" alt=\"tuvien2-1778234642.jpg\" width=\"555\" height=\"370\"></a></figure><div class=\"desc_cation\" style=\"margin:0px auto;max-width:680px;padding:15px 0px 0px;text-align:left;\">The remaining structure is where the monks used to live. Photo: Quốc Lê</div></div></div></div></div></figure></div></div><div class=\"section-inner inset-column\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial, serif;font-size:20px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;margin:0px auto;max-width:710px;padding:0px 15px;text-align:left;width:710px;word-spacing:0px;\"><p style=\"font-family:Arial;line-height:32px;margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;\">Located by Long Thành Bay, Citeaux Mỹ Ca Monastery was once a famous Catholic architectural structure in Vietnam during the colonial period, designed in the Gothic style. The structure was built in 1934 and completed after four years, serving as a residence for monks. To access this place, the monks had only one way: by boat. Later, due to the impact of the war, the entire monastery had to relocate to another location and has been abandoned ever since. Visitors can see the monastery from the access road to Long Thành Airport.</p><p style=\"font-family:Arial;line-height:32px;margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;\"><b style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>Cam Lâm Mango Orchard</strong></b></p></div><p><img style=\"font-size:0px;line-height:0;margin:0px;max-width:100%;padding:0px;\" src=\"https://i1-dulich.vnecdn.net/2026/05/08/xoai-1778239102-5942-1778258996.webp?w=0&amp;h=0&amp;q=100&amp;dpr=1&amp;fit=crop&amp;s=1EMhJpOtCt7SZ1fK26LwTw\" alt=\"\" width=\"730\" height=\"548\"></p><div class=\"section-inner inset-column\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial, serif;font-size:20px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;margin:0px auto;max-width:710px;padding:0px 15px;text-align:left;width:710px;word-spacing:0px;\"><div class=\"medium-insert-images\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;text-align:center;\"><figure style=\"margin:0px;max-width:100%;padding:0px;\"><figcaption style=\"color:rgb(79,79,79);font-family:arial;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;line-height:27.2px;margin:0px auto;max-width:670px;padding:10px 0px 0px;text-align:left;\">Visitors exploring the Cam Lâm mango orchard. Photo: <i style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;\">Trần Hoài</i></figcaption></figure></div><p style=\"font-family:Arial;line-height:32px;margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;\">Cam Lâm is considered a major mango-growing region in Bà Rịa - Vũng Tàu, with thousands of hectares and many varieties from Australia or Hòa Lộc and Canh Nông mangoes. The best season for visits is usually from around April to July, when the orchards are in harvest. Visitors can tour the orchards, learn about planting and care, and pick mangoes themselves. These areas also sell mango specialties such as Cam Lâm mango cakes, dried mango, mango tea, and fresh mangoes.</p><p style=\"font-family:Arial;line-height:32px;margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;\">The mango orchards are located in Cam Hải Tây or Cam Đức, 10 to 20 km from Bai Dai, depending on the area. Travel time is about 20 to 30 minutes. Note that when visiting, it is advisable to wear flat shoes.</p></div><div class=\"section-inner inset-column\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial, serif;font-size:20px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;margin:0px auto;max-width:710px;padding:0px 15px;text-align:left;width:710px;word-spacing:0px;\"><h3 class=\"e345d5012881b290698d\" style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial, sans-serif;font-size:26px;line-height:1.313;margin:0px 0px 1.05263rem;min-height:1px;padding:0px;text-align:center;\"><strong>Note</strong></h3><p style=\"font-family:Arial;line-height:32px;margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;\">Long Thành is drier and hotter than Vũng Tàu, especially from April to August. Visitors should prepare sunscreen, sunglasses, light jackets, and drink plenty of water.</p><p style=\"font-family:Arial;line-height:32px;margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;\">Bai Dai is beautiful but has sections with strong waves and currents. Be cautious not to swim too far out.</p></div><p><img class=\"image_resized\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1920/1439;font-size:0px;line-height:0;margin:0px;max-width:100%;padding:0px;width:1100px;\" src=\"https://i1-dulich.vnecdn.net/2026/05/08/bai-dai-CR-1778239747-8028-1778258996.jpg?w=0&amp;h=0&amp;q=100&amp;dpr=1&amp;fit=crop&amp;s=3mq-m-G02l-KWdzapOFgiQ\" alt=\"\" width=\"1920\" height=\"1439\"></p><div class=\"section-inner outset-column\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial, serif;font-size:20px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;margin:0px auto;max-width:1130px;padding:0px 15px;text-align:left;width:1130px;word-spacing:0px;\"><div class=\"medium-insert-images medium-insert-images-large\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;text-align:center;\"><figure style=\"margin:0px;max-width:100%;padding:0px;\"><figcaption style=\"color:rgb(79,79,79);font-family:arial;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;line-height:27.2px;margin:0px auto;max-width:670px;padding:10px 0px 0px;text-align:left;\">Long Thành is beautiful, but visitors should be aware of strong currents. Photo: <i style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;\">Alex</i></figcaption></figure></div></div><div class=\"section-inner inset-column\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial, serif;font-size:20px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;margin:0px auto;max-width:710px;padding:0px 15px;text-align:left;width:710px;word-spacing:0px;\"><p style=\"font-family:Arial;line-height:32px;margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;\">The coastal resorts are extensive but have fewer walking and entertainment areas compared to central Vũng Tàu. The distances between attractions are quite far. To dine and enjoy activities, visitors should rent a motorbike or car.</p><p style=\"font-family:Arial;line-height:32px;margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;\">Ride-hailing taxis are not abundant, and booking a ride can take time, so visitors need to prepare in advance.</p><p style=\"font-family:Arial;line-height:32px;margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;\">Long Thành is more focused on relaxation, so the evenings are quite peaceful. If visitors prefer a lively atmosphere, they can explore entertainment areas near Vũng Tàu or at the bars in the resorts.</p><p style=\"font-family:Arial;line-height:32px;margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;\">Source: according to vnexpress</p></div>', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1610641818989-c2051b5e2cfd?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&h=927&q=80');
INSERT INTO `posts_translations` (`lang_code`, `posts_id`, `name`, `description`, `content`, `image`) VALUES
('en_US', 66, 'Top 5 Best Sauna Services in Vũng Tàu', 'Discover the top 5 best sauna services in Vũng Tàu featuring a premium relaxation environment, dry sauna, wet sauna, jacuzzi, and international standard wellness. From the luxurious sea-view sauna at Ruby 68 to the Korean sauna Aquafield, these are the ideal spots to rejuvenate your energy while traveling in Vũng Tàu.', '<p><strong>Top 5 Best Sauna Services in Vũng Tàu</strong></p><p>After a long day exploring the azure waters of Vũng Tàu, nothing is more delightful than relaxing in the warm sauna ambiance to rejuvenate your energy and revitalize your body. Not only is sauna a beloved wellness trend in Europe, South Korea, and Japan, but it is increasingly becoming a favored relaxation experience for many travelers visiting Vũng Tàu.</p><p>Here are the top 5 outstanding sauna locations in Vũng Tàu for tourists, vacationers, and health enthusiasts.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>1. Ruby 68 Hotel – 3-Star Ocean View Sauna &amp; Jacuzzi</strong></p><p><strong>Reference price:</strong> 250,000 VND/person/visit</p><figure class=\"image\"><img style=\"aspect-ratio:2000/1409;\" src=\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1631889993959-41b4e9c6e3c5?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1600&q=80\" alt=\"18.png\" width=\"2000\" height=\"1409\"></figure><p>Located on the 7th floor of Ruby 68 Hotel, the Sauna &amp; Jacuzzi area offers a private and luxurious relaxation experience with:</p><p><span><img class=\"image_resized\" style=\"aspect-ratio:468/330;width:100%;\" src=\"/storage/image-4.png\" alt=\"image-4.png\" width=\"468\" height=\"330\"></span></p><ul style=\"list-style-type:disc;\"><li>Dry sauna</li><li>Wet sauna</li><li>Hot &amp; cold Jacuzzi</li><li>Separate male &amp; female areas</li><li>Personal lockers and fully equipped changing rooms</li></ul><figure class=\"image\"><img style=\"aspect-ratio:1918/1284;\" src=\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1470337458703-46ad1756a187?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1600&q=80\" alt=\"3.png\" width=\"1918\" height=\"1284\"></figure><p><span>&nbsp;</span> What sets Ruby 68 apart is the wellness space combined with an infinity pool overlooking the sea, creating a truly luxurious relaxation experience. This is also one of the saunas favored by many international guests, especially those from Russia and Europe, in Vũng Tàu.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>2. Champa Island Vũng Tàu – Affordable Sauna for Locals &amp; Tourists</strong></p><p><strong>Reference price:</strong> approximately 120,000 – 150,000 VND/visit</p><p><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, sans-serif;font-size:12pt;\"><img class=\"image_resized\" style=\"aspect-ratio:468/300;width:95.15%;\" src=\"/storage/image-7.jpeg\" alt=\"CHAMPA SPA – Champa Island Vũng Tàu - Resort Hotel &amp; Spa\" width=\"468\" height=\"300\"></span></p><p>Champa Island features a sauna and steam bath located within the gym-spa complex of the resort. With quite accessible pricing, this is a suitable choice for guests wanting to experience a basic sauna in a tranquil and relaxing environment.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>3. Aquafield Vũng Tàu – Large-Scale Korean Standard Sauna</strong></p><p><strong>Reference price:</strong> approximately 450,000 – 600,000 VND/person</p><p><span><img class=\"image_resized\" style=\"aspect-ratio:468/312;width:100%;\" src=\"/storage/image-3.jpeg\" alt=\"Aquafield Vũng Tàu – Premium Spa &amp; Sauna Complex, the First Top 1 Korean Standard in Vietnam – Hồ Mây Park\" width=\"468\" height=\"312\"></span></p><p>Aquafield is a prominent Korean jjimjilbang complex in Vũng Tàu with various themed sauna areas:</p><ul style=\"list-style-type:disc;\"><li>Himalayan salt room</li><li>Activated charcoal sauna</li><li>Snow room</li><li>Steam room</li><li>Large relaxation area</li></ul><p>This is an ideal choice for guests who love Korean sauna culture and modern wellness experiences.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>4. Vesna Hotel Vũng Tàu – Centrally Located Affordable Sauna</strong></p><p><strong>Reference price:</strong> approximately 150,000 – 200,000 VND/visit</p><p><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, sans-serif;font-size:12pt;\"><img src=\"/storage/image-6.jpeg\" alt=\"Vesna Hotel Vũng Tàu\" width=\"341\" height=\"512\"></span></p><p>Situated near Tran Phu beach, Vesna Hotel is perfect for guests looking to unwind quickly after swimming or exercising. The sauna here is reasonably priced and convenient for guests staying in the city center.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>5. Galina Mud Bath &amp; Spa – Sauna Combined with Spa &amp; Mud Bath</strong></p><p><strong>Reference price:</strong> from approximately 300,000 VND/combo</p><p><span><img class=\"image_resized\" style=\"aspect-ratio:468/246;width:100%;\" src=\"/storage/image-2.jpeg\" alt=\"Mud Bath at Galina Hotel &amp; Spa - Klook Vietnam\" width=\"468\" height=\"246\"></span></p><p>Galina is a familiar destination for Russian guests and international travelers thanks to its combined model:</p><ul style=\"list-style-type:disc;\"><li>Sauna</li><li>Steam bath</li><li>Mud bath</li><li>Relaxation massage</li></ul><p>The space features a traditional spa style, suitable for guests wanting to combine health care and relaxation in a comprehensive treatment.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Why Do Many Travelers Love Sauna?</strong></p><p>Sauna not only helps with relaxation but also offers numerous health benefits:</p><ul style=\"list-style-type:disc;\"><li>Supports stress reduction</li><li>Relaxes muscles</li><li>Supports blood circulation</li><li>Helps improve sleep quality</li><li>Enhances recovery after exercise and travel</li></ul><p>Especially for travelers from Russia, South Korea, Japan, and Europe, sauna has almost become an indispensable part of the relaxation experience.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Experience Premium Sauna in Vũng Tàu</strong></p><p>If you are seeking a true relaxation space after busy days, the sauna services in Vũng Tàu will undoubtedly provide a more fulfilling relaxation experience.</p><p>At Ruby 68 Hotel, the Sauna &amp; Jacuzzi area is not just a place to unwind, but also a journey to restore energy amidst the inspiring oceanic scenery of Vũng Tàu.</p><p>&nbsp;</p>', NULL),
('en_US', 67, 'Vũng Tàu \"Explosive” Series of Cultural and Artistic Events in Summer 2026', 'In the summer of 2026, Ba Ria - Vung Tau will explode with the Ocean Festival \"Colors of the Ocean - Reaching International Heights\" and a series of world-class music festivals. Choose Ruby 68 Hotel Vũng Tàu as your luxurious stopover to fully enjoy the vibrant festival atmosphere and the exclusive experience of a 3-star beachfront retreat. Discover the essence of summer now!', '<p style=\"background-color:rgb(252,250,246);color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Newsreader, serif;font-size:20px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;list-style-type:none;margin:0px 0px 25px;padding:0px;text-align:justify;word-spacing:0px;\"><span style=\"font-family:unset;list-style-type:none;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;list-style-type:none;margin:0px;padding:0px;\">From late May to the end of July, Ba Ria - Vung Tau province will host a series of large-scale, high-class cultural and artistic events. This series of activities promises to bring residents and visitors explosive emotional experiences in the vibrant and bustling summer atmosphere.</strong></span></p><p style=\"background-color:rgb(252,250,246);color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Newsreader, serif;font-size:20px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;list-style-type:none;margin:0px 0px 25px;padding:0px;text-align:justify;word-spacing:0px;\"><span style=\"font-family:unset;list-style-type:none;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;list-style-type:none;margin:0px;padding:0px;\">Shining a Light on Ba Ria - Vung Tau Culture</strong></span></p><p style=\"background-color:rgb(252,250,246);color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Newsreader, serif;font-size:20px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;list-style-type:none;margin:0px 0px 25px;padding:0px;text-align:justify;word-spacing:0px;\"><span style=\"font-family:unset;list-style-type:none;margin:0px;padding:0px;\">This summer, Ba Ria - Vung Tau will be the focal point with two major cultural events, prominently featuring the Ba Ria - Vung Tau Sea Festival 2026 and the 6th Cham Ethnic Culture Festival. The 6th Cham Ethnic Culture Festival, organized in collaboration with the Ministry of Culture, Sports and Tourism and the Ba Ria - Vung Tau Provincial People\'s Committee, will take place from June 26 to 28, under the theme “Preserving and Promoting Cham Ethnic Cultural Identity in the New Era.” The festival will gather approximately 700 artisans, performers, and athletes from the Cham ethnic community across 7 provinces and cities: Ba Ria - Vung Tau, Gia Lai, Dak Lak, Lam Dong, An Giang, Tay Ninh, and Ho Chi Minh City. In addition to the opening ceremony (evening of June 26) and closing ceremony (evening of June 28), the festival will feature numerous activities and events such as: performances showcasing excerpts from traditional Cham cultural rituals; exhibitions promoting traditional Cham culture; demonstrations of traditional Cham crafts; community art festivals; displays of Cham ethnic costumes; sports competitions and traditional games of the Cham people; a seminar on “Preserving and Promoting the Cultural Heritage of Cham in Ba Ria - Vung Tau Associated with Sustainable Tourism Development”; and exhibitions introducing tourism products, OCOP products, and specialty products of Ba Ria - Vung Tau province... Cultural, artistic, and exhibition activities will be held at the April 16 Square (Phan Rang and Dong Hai wards). Sports events and traditional games will take place at the Provincial Sports Competition Service Center (Bao An ward).</span></p><div style=\"background-color:rgb(252,250,246);color:rgb(38,35,56);font-family:Newsreader, serif;font-size:20px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;list-style-type:none;margin:0px;padding:0px;word-spacing:0px;\"><figure class=\"table\" style=\"width:702.328px;\"><table class=\"image center\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse;margin:0px auto 10px;max-width:100%;padding:0px;\" align=\"center\"><tbody style=\"list-style-type:none;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><tr style=\"border-style:solid;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><td style=\"border-style:solid;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><div class=\"new\" style=\"background-color:transparent;font-size:20px;list-style-type:none;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><div class=\"new\" style=\"background-color:transparent;font-size:20px;list-style-type:none;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><div class=\"new\" style=\"background-color:transparent;font-size:20px;list-style-type:none;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><div class=\"new\" style=\"background-color:transparent;font-size:20px;list-style-type:none;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><img class=\"image_resized\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1500/1000;height:auto;list-style-type:none;margin:0px;max-width:100%;padding:0px;width:702.328px;\" src=\"https://baokhanhhoa.vn/file/e7837c02857c8ca30185a8c39b582c03/052026/img_1287_20260517043823_20260517191821.jpg\" alt=\"Cham folk dance performance at April 2 Square.\" width=\"1500\" height=\"1000\"></div></div></div></div></td></tr><tr style=\"border-style:solid;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><td class=\"desc\" style=\"background-color:rgb(251,250,249);border-style:solid;color:rgb(14,107,145);margin:0px;padding:0px;text-align:center;\">Cham folk dance performance at April 2 Square.</td></tr></tbody></table></figure></div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(252,250,246);color:rgb(38,35,56);font-family:Newsreader, serif;font-size:20px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;list-style-type:none;margin:0px;padding:0px;word-spacing:0px;\"><figure class=\"table\" style=\"width:702.328px;\"><table class=\"image center\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse;margin:0px auto 10px;max-width:100%;padding:0px;\" align=\"center\"><tbody style=\"list-style-type:none;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><tr style=\"border-style:solid;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><td style=\"border-style:solid;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><div class=\"new\" style=\"background-color:transparent;font-size:20px;list-style-type:none;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><div class=\"new\" style=\"background-color:transparent;font-size:20px;list-style-type:none;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><div class=\"new\" style=\"background-color:transparent;font-size:20px;list-style-type:none;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><div class=\"new\" style=\"background-color:transparent;font-size:20px;list-style-type:none;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><img class=\"image_resized\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1920/1245;height:auto;list-style-type:none;margin:0px;max-width:100%;padding:0px;width:702.328px;\" src=\"https://baokhanhhoa.vn/file/e7837c02857c8ca30185a8c39b582c03/052026/img_1964_20260517043347_20260517191709.jpg\" alt=\"The Vũng Tàu Carnival program during the 2025 Sea Culture - Tourism Festival.\" width=\"1920\" height=\"1245\"></div></div></div></div></td></tr><tr style=\"border-style:solid;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><td class=\"desc\" style=\"background-color:rgb(251,250,249);border-style:solid;color:rgb(14,107,145);margin:0px;padding:0px;text-align:center;\">The Vũng Tàu Carnival program during the 2025 Sea Culture - Tourism Festival.</td></tr></tbody></table></figure></div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(252,250,246);color:rgb(38,35,56);font-family:Newsreader, serif;font-size:20px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;list-style-type:none;margin:0px;padding:0px;word-spacing:0px;\"><p style=\"background-color:transparent;color:rgb(0,0,0);list-style-type:none;margin:0px 0px 25px;padding:0px;text-align:justify;\"><span style=\"font-family:unset;list-style-type:none;margin:0px;padding:0px;\">The Ba Ria - Vung Tau Sea Festival 2026, organized by the Provincial People\'s Committee, themed “Ocean Colors - Reaching International Heights,” will officially take place from July 17 to 19 at April 2 Square (Vũng Tàu ward) and several other locations across the province. Key events include: the opening ceremony (evening of July 17); the Carnival festival - a parade of floral floats themed “Vũng Tàu Sea Flowers” (afternoon of July 18); the finals of the Vietnam Supermodel and Mister Vietnam 2026, combined with a fashion and music show “Runway to the World” (evening of July 18); and the closing ceremony and international music festival&nbsp;</span></p><div style=\"background-color:transparent;font-size:20px;list-style-type:none;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><figure class=\"table\" style=\"width:702.328px;\"><table class=\"image center\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse;margin:0px auto 10px;max-width:100%;padding:0px;\" align=\"center\"><tbody style=\"list-style-type:none;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><tr style=\"border-style:solid;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><td style=\"border-style:solid;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><div class=\"new\" style=\"background-color:transparent;font-size:20px;list-style-type:none;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><div class=\"new\" style=\"background-color:transparent;font-size:20px;list-style-type:none;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><div class=\"new\" style=\"background-color:transparent;font-size:20px;list-style-type:none;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><div class=\"new\" style=\"background-color:transparent;font-size:20px;list-style-type:none;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><img class=\"image_resized\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1920/1280;height:auto;list-style-type:none;margin:0px;max-width:100%;padding:0px;width:702.328px;\" src=\"https://baokhanhhoa.vn/file/e7837c02857c8ca30185a8c39b582c03/052026/img_1892_20260517043329_20260517191739.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"1920\" height=\"1280\"></div></div></div></div></td></tr><tr style=\"border-style:solid;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><td class=\"desc\" style=\"background-color:rgb(251,250,249);border-style:solid;color:rgb(14,107,145);margin:0px;padding:0px;text-align:center;\">&nbsp;</td></tr></tbody></table></figure></div><p style=\"background-color:transparent;color:rgb(0,0,0);list-style-type:none;margin:0px 0px 25px;padding:0px;text-align:justify;\"><span style=\"font-family:unset;list-style-type:none;margin:0px;padding:0px;\">In addition to the main activities and events, from July 10 to August 10, the Ba Ria - Vung Tau Sea Festival 2026 will feature numerous national-scale activities and events, with participation from various central ministries, domestic provinces and cities, and countries that have cooperative relations with Ba Ria - Vung Tau province. With nearly 30 activities and events taking place consecutively over a month, it will provide residents and visitors with diverse and unique experiences of the land and people of Ba Ria - Vung Tau.</span></p><div style=\"background-color:transparent;font-size:20px;list-style-type:none;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" id=\"blockquote2\"><blockquote style=\"background-color:rgb(237,237,237);border-style:solid;color:rgb(85,85,85);font-size:1rem;line-height:1.4;list-style-type:none;margin:20px auto;padding:1em 20px 1em 50px;\"><p style=\"background-color:transparent;color:rgb(0,0,0);list-style-type:none;margin:0px;padding:0px;text-align:justify;\"><i><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;list-style-type:none;margin:0px;padding:0px;\">Ms. THAI THI LE HANG - Director of the Department of Culture, Sports and Tourism</strong>: The two major cultural events, the Ba Ria - Vung Tau Sea Festival 2026 and the 6th Cham Ethnic Culture Festival, will contribute to enhancing exchanges with friends both domestically and internationally; spreading the cultural identity of Ba Ria - Vung Tau; promoting the local image; and attracting tourists. It is expected that the Ba Ria - Vung Tau Sea Festival will attract between 600,000 to 800,000 local residents and both domestic and international visitors. To ensure the success of these two events, the Provincial People\'s Committee requires that cultural, sports, tourism, and artistic exchange activities must be distinctive, rich, and diverse, with the participation of many forces and renowned artists; creating many impressive tourism products; contributing to the socio-economic growth index of the province.</i></p></blockquote></div><p style=\"background-color:transparent;color:rgb(0,0,0);list-style-type:none;margin:0px 0px 25px;padding:0px;text-align:justify;\"><span style=\"font-family:unset;list-style-type:none;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;list-style-type:none;margin:0px;padding:0px;\">World-Class Music Festivals</strong></span></p><p style=\"background-color:transparent;color:rgb(0,0,0);list-style-type:none;margin:0px 0px 25px;padding:0px;text-align:justify;\"><span style=\"font-family:unset;list-style-type:none;margin:0px;padding:0px;\">The Provincial People\'s Committee has also recently issued a document agreeing to allow Sun Ba Ria - Vung Tau Co., Ltd. to organize a grand music festival themed “Mega Booming Charmora City - Awakening the Heart of Vũng Tàu Downtown.” The event is scheduled to take place on June 13 at April 2 Square. With a large and magnificent stage, gathering renowned domestic and international artists, the event will be an attractive entertainment highlight drawing a large number of residents and visitors.</span></p><figure class=\"table\" style=\"width:702.328px;\"><table class=\"image center\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse;margin:0px auto 10px;max-width:100%;padding:0px;\" align=\"center\"><tbody style=\"list-style-type:none;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><tr style=\"border-style:solid;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><td style=\"border-style:solid;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><div class=\"new\" style=\"background-color:transparent;font-size:20px;list-style-type:none;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><div class=\"new\" style=\"background-color:transparent;font-size:20px;list-style-type:none;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><div class=\"new\" style=\"background-color:transparent;font-size:20px;list-style-type:none;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><div class=\"new\" style=\"background-color:transparent;font-size:20px;list-style-type:none;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><img class=\"image_resized\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1920/1277;height:auto;list-style-type:none;margin:0px;max-width:100%;padding:0px;width:702.328px;\" src=\"https://baokhanhhoa.vn/file/e7837c02857c8ca30185a8c39b582c03/052026/vth_0789_20260517043435_20260517191638.jpg\" alt=\"Singer Duc Phuc performing at a grand music festival held at April 2 Square.\" width=\"1920\" height=\"1277\"></div></div></div></div></td></tr><tr style=\"border-style:solid;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><td class=\"desc\" style=\"background-color:rgb(251,250,249);border-style:solid;color:rgb(14,107,145);margin:0px;padding:0px;text-align:center;\">Singer Duc Phuc performing at a grand music festival held at April 2 Square.</td></tr></tbody></table></figure></div><p style=\"background-color:rgb(252,250,246);color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Newsreader, serif;font-size:20px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;list-style-type:none;margin:0px 0px 25px;padding:0px;text-align:justify;word-spacing:0px;\"><span style=\"font-family:unset;list-style-type:none;margin:0px;padding:0px;\">The highlight of the music festival will be a 15-minute artistic fireworks display concluding the program, featuring 500 low-altitude fireworks and 1,000 high-altitude fireworks. According to the leadership of Sun Ba Ria - Vung Tau, “Mega Booming Charmora City - Awakening the Heart of Vũng Tàu Downtown” aims to enrich tourism products serving the people and visitors during the summer tourism season of 2026; while also promoting and enhancing the image and brand of Ba Ria - Vung Tau tourism to visitors, especially investors in choosing locations for organizing national and international events.</span></p><p style=\"background-color:rgb(252,250,246);color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Newsreader, serif;font-size:20px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;list-style-type:none;margin:0px 0px 25px;padding:0px;text-align:justify;word-spacing:0px;\"><span style=\"font-family:unset;list-style-type:none;margin:0px;padding:0px;\">Following the event “Mega Booming Charmora City - Awakening the Heart of Vũng Tàu Downtown,” a consortium of Century Investment and Advertising Joint Stock Company and Inspike Communication Co., Ltd. (Ho Chi Minh City) will organize a series of two large-scale summer music festivals at April 2 Square in June. Specifically, the music night “Red Bull - Determination to the End” will take place on the evening of June 20, featuring young artists such as: Rhyder, Osad, My My, and Fire Band; followed by the program “Play Together - Connecting Vietnamese Identity” on the evening of June 27 with the participation of Tieu Minh Phung, Orange, Quan AP, Lamoon Diem Hang, Min... Attendees will not only immerse themselves in the explosive musical atmosphere but also have the opportunity to participate in engaging experiential activities and interactive mini-games at booths within the square.</span> &nbsp;<br><br>Source of information from Ba Ria - Vung Tau Online newspaper</p>', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1613977257363-707ba9348227?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&h=927&q=80'),
('en_US', 68, 'Top 10 Most Beautiful Infinity Pools in Vũng Tàu 2026 | Must-Visit Check-in Spots', 'Discover the top 10 most beautiful infinity pools in Vũng Tàu, featuring breathtaking ocean views, luxurious relaxation spaces, and stunning photo spots for beach-loving travelers.', '<h1>Top 10 Most Beautiful Infinity Pools in Vũng Tàu – Paradise Retreats Amidst Sea and Sky</h1><h2>Vũng Tàu – The city of the most stunning infinity pools in Vietnam</h2><p>Renowned not only for its crystal-clear beaches and temperate climate year-round, Vũng Tàu is also regarded as a relaxation paradise with a plethora of hotels and resorts featuring breathtaking infinity pools. Here, guests can immerse themselves in the refreshing waters, gaze at the vast ocean, and capture unforgettable moments in one of the most beautiful bays in the world.</p><p>If you are searching for a location that offers both relaxation and stunning check-in spots, let us explore the top 10 most beautiful infinity pools in Vũng Tàu below.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><h2>1. Ruby 68 Hotel – Transparent Glass Pool Overlooking Back Beach Vung Tau</h2><p>Situated on the 7th floor of Ruby 68 Hotel, the infinity pool is one of the standout features of this 3-star hotel brand in Vũng Tàu.</p><figure class=\"image\"><img style=\"aspect-ratio:2000/1333;\" src=\"/storage/image-10.png\" alt=\"image-10.png\" width=\"2000\" height=\"1333\"></figure><p>What sets this pool apart is its modern transparent glass design combined with a panoramic view of Back Beach Vung Tau. From here, guests can admire the beauty of the blue sea, Yen Island, and the endless horizon.</p><figure class=\"image\"><img style=\"aspect-ratio:2048/1366;\" src=\"/storage/image-11.png\" alt=\"image-11.png\" width=\"2048\" height=\"1366\"></figure><p>On clear days, the water reflects the blue sky, creating a stunning scene. As the sun sets, the golden rays cast over the sea, forming a captivating natural painting.</p><figure class=\"image\"><img style=\"aspect-ratio:1080/1216;\" src=\"/storage/image-9.png\" alt=\"image-9.png\" width=\"1080\" height=\"1216\"></figure><p>Right in the pool area is the Ruby Ocean Bar, serving a variety of tropical cocktails, fresh fruit juices, and light snacks. This is the ideal spot to unwind after a day of exploring the coastal city.</p><p><strong>Highlights</strong></p><ul><li>Infinity pool with a unique transparent glass design</li><li>Panoramic view of Back Beach Vung Tau</li><li>Ruby Ocean Bar located right in the pool area</li><li>Ideal space for watching the sunrise and sunset</li><li>Suitable for both relaxation guests and photography enthusiasts</li></ul><h2>2. InterContinental Vũng Tàu</h2><p>Located on Tran Phu Street, InterContinental Vũng Tàu boasts a luxurious infinity pool with stunning sea views.</p><figure class=\"image\"><img style=\"aspect-ratio:2200/1200;\" src=\"https://nhatrang.intercontinental.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/100/2025/05/Pool-2-3.jpg\" alt=\"Amenities - InterContinental Vũng Tàu\" width=\"2200\" height=\"1200\"></figure><p>The modern design and open space allow guests to fully enjoy the beauty of Back Beach Vung Tau right in the heart of the city. The pool is surrounded by premium sun loungers and a professional beverage service area.</p><p>This is a favorite choice among many international travelers due to its convenient location and top-notch service quality.</p><h2>3. Sheraton Vũng Tàu Hotel &amp; Spa</h2><p>Sheraton Vũng Tàu is famous for its outdoor pool facing the sea, located on the upper floors of the hotel.</p><figure class=\"image\"><img style=\"aspect-ratio:1000/563;\" src=\"https://mia.vn/media/uploads/blog-du-lich/top-4-khach-san-nha-trang-co-ho-boi-vo-cuc-dep-xuat-sac--1660675796.jpg\" alt=\"Top 4 Hotels in Vũng Tàu with Outstanding Infinity Pools 2\" width=\"1000\" height=\"563\"></figure><p>The pool area features a modern style with a direct view of the East Sea. In the afternoon, it becomes one of the best spots to watch the sunset in central Vũng Tàu.</p><h2>4. Hồ Mây Park Resort Vũng Tàu</h2><p>Located on Hon Tre Island, Hồ Mây Park Resort features a vast infinity pool set against a backdrop of lush nature.</p><figure class=\"image\"><img style=\"aspect-ratio:1280/853;\" src=\"https://vinpearlresortvietnam.com/wp-content/uploads/nghi-duong-tai-Vinpearl-Luxury-Nha-Trang-07-1.jpg\" alt=\"Discover the Infinity Pool at Hồ Mây Park Vũng Tàu – A Premium Relaxation Experience - Hồ Mây Park Resorts &amp; Hotels\" width=\"1280\" height=\"853\"></figure><p>From the pool, guests can gaze out over the clear sea and distant mountain ranges, creating a rare peaceful scene.</p><p>This is the ideal choice for those seeking a private retreat amidst nature.</p><h2>5. Hồ Mây Park Luxury Vũng Tàu</h2><p>If you appreciate luxury and prestige, the infinity pool at Hồ Mây Park Luxury Vũng Tàu will surely satisfy you.</p><figure class=\"image\"><img style=\"aspect-ratio:1024/683;\" src=\"https://cf.bstatic.com/xdata/images/hotel/max1024x768/10537303.jpg?k=10e954dd15f8eec110df88df36bb908bd8f4b6c2a1bd265c88b6b7642b259607&amp;o=\" alt=\"Pool in/near Hồ Mây Park Luxury Vũng Tàu\" width=\"1024\" height=\"683\"></figure><p>The harmonious design between modern architecture and natural landscapes provides guests with an absolute sense of relaxation.</p><h2>6. Havana Vũng Tàu Hotel</h2><p>As one of the prominent hotels on Tran Phu Street, Havana features an infinity pool with a direct view of the sea.</p><figure class=\"image\"><img style=\"aspect-ratio:1024/403;\" src=\"https://havanahotel.vn/storage/dich-cua-ban/at-your-services-pool.jpeg\" alt=\"POOL - 3-Star Hotel Havana Vũng Tàu\" width=\"1024\" height=\"403\"></figure><p>This location is favored by many travelers due to its convenient position, spacious environment, and the ability to enjoy panoramic views of Vũng Tàu&#039;s coastline.</p><h2>7. Citadines Bayfront Vũng Tàu</h2><p>The pool at Citadines Bayfront is situated at a high position, facing directly towards the central beach.</p><figure class=\"image image_resized\" style=\"width:98.17%;\"><img style=\"aspect-ratio:700/467;\" src=\"https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/10/81/88/b8/citadines-bayfront-nha.jpg?w=700&amp;h=-1&amp;s=1\" alt=\"Citadines Bayfront Vũng Tàu Pool: Images and Reviews - Tripadvisor\" width=\"700\" height=\"467\"></figure><p>The modern space with minimalist design makes it a favorite spot for many young travelers and social media enthusiasts.</p><h2>8. Meliá Hồ Mây Park Vũng Tàu Empire</h2><p>Located right in the city center, the infinity pool at Meliá Hồ Mây Park Vũng Tàu Empire offers a modern relaxation experience with a comprehensive view of the entire city.</p><figure class=\"image\"><img style=\"aspect-ratio:1280/853;\" src=\"https://vinpearlresortvietnam.com/wp-content/uploads/Vinpearl-Empire-Nha-Trang-Ho-boi-vo-cuc.jpg\" alt=\"Melia Hồ Mây Park Empire Vũng Tàu Hotel - Room Rates 2026\" width=\"1280\" height=\"853\"></figure><p>At night, the sparkling lights from the tall buildings create an incredibly impressive scene.</p><h2>9. Queen Ann Vũng Tàu Hotel</h2><p>Queen Ann features an infinity pool located on a high floor with stunning sea views.</p><figure class=\"image\"><img style=\"aspect-ratio:920/600;\" src=\"https://queenannvungtau.com/uploads/contents/images/b%C3%A0i%20vi%E1%BA%BFt%20h%E1%BB%93%20b%C6%A1i%20ng%C6%B0%E1%BB%9Di%20l%E1%BB%9Bn%201.jpg\" alt=\"Queenannvungtau.com\" width=\"920\" height=\"600\"></figure><p>The tranquil atmosphere and exquisite design make it a suitable choice for couples or travelers seeking privacy.</p><h2>10. Panorama Vũng Tàu</h2><p>Panorama is one of the most prominent buildings in central Vũng Tàu.</p><figure class=\"image\"><img style=\"aspect-ratio:960/640;\" src=\"https://content.skyscnr.com/available/2409577003/2409577003_WxH.jpg\" alt=\"Panorama Wins Residences Vũng Tàu Hotel, Vũng Tàu - Skyscanner\" width=\"960\" height=\"640\"></figure><p>The infinity pool here boasts an expansive view encompassing the entire city and the blue sea in front, creating stunning check-in photo opportunities.</p><h2>Why is the infinity pool an unmissable experience when visiting Vũng Tàu?</h2><p>Unlike traditional pools, infinity pools are designed to create a visual effect that makes the water appear to merge with the horizon. When combined with the stunning natural scenery of Back Beach Vung Tau, this experience becomes even more special.</p><p>Not only a place for relaxation, the infinity pool is also an ideal spot to:</p><ul><li>Watch the sunrise over the sea</li><li>Enjoy cocktails by the pool</li><li>Take stunning photos</li><li>Indulge in a luxurious retreat</li><li>Relax with family and friends</li></ul><h2>Which infinity pool is the most beautiful in Vũng Tàu?</h2><p>Each pool on the list possesses its own unique beauty.</p><p>While Hồ Mây Park stands out with its island resort space, InterContinental scores points for its central location, Ruby 68 Hotel makes a mark with its unique transparent glass pool and panoramic view of Back Beach Vung Tau from above.</p><p>Regardless of which destination you choose, an afternoon of relaxation by the infinity pool, watching the sunset gradually descend over the sea will undoubtedly be an unforgettable experience in your journey to explore Vũng Tàu.</p>', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551882547-ff40c63fe5fa?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&h=927&q=80'),
('en_US', 69, 'Discover Northern Vũng Tàu - A New Generation Coastal Destination in Ba Ria - Vung Tau', 'Not only does Vũng Tàu boast crystal-clear waters and gentle waves lapping at the shore, but the northern region is also becoming the focal point of international media attention. Publications such as Luxury Travel Magazine and The Manila Times have dubbed it a \"new generation beach destination,\" where natural beauty and local culture intertwine to create unique experiences.', '<div class=\"content-detail cate_F1CD6477B2312B69E053047A900A073C\" style=\"background-color:rgb(252,250,246);color:rgb(38,35,56);font-family:Newsreader, serif;font-size:20px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;line-height:32px;list-style-type:none;margin:0px;padding:0px;word-spacing:0px;\" id=\"content\"><div class=\"td-post-content tagdiv-type\" style=\"background-color:transparent;font-size:20px;list-style-type:none;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><p style=\"background-color:transparent;color:rgb(0,0,0);list-style-type:none;margin:0px 0px 25px;padding:0px;text-align:justify;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;list-style-type:none;margin:0px;padding:0px;\">Not only does it boast crystal-clear waters and gentle waves lapping at the shore, but the northern region of Vũng Tàu is becoming the focal point of international media attention. Publications such as Luxury Travel Magazine and The Manila Times refer to it as a &quot;new generation coastal destination,&quot; where natural beauty and local culture intertwine to create unique experiences.</strong></p><div style=\"background-color:transparent;font-size:20px;list-style-type:none;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><figure class=\"table\" style=\"width:702.328px;\"><table class=\"image center\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse;margin:0px auto 10px;max-width:100%;padding:0px;text-align:center;\" align=\"center\"><tbody style=\"list-style-type:none;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><tr style=\"border-style:solid;border-width:0px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><td style=\"border-style:solid;border-width:0px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><div class=\"new\" style=\"background-color:transparent;font-size:20px;list-style-type:none;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><figure class=\"image image_resized\" style=\"height:auto;width:702.328px;\"><img style=\"aspect-ratio:1536/1024;list-style-type:none;margin:0px;max-width:100%;padding:0px;\" src=\"https://baokhanhhoa.vn/file/e7837c02857c8ca30185a8c39b582c03/052026/copilot_20260526_213230_20260526213249.png\" alt=\"copilot_20260526_213230_20260526213249.png\" width=\"1536\" height=\"1024\"></figure></div></td></tr><tr style=\"border-style:solid;border-width:0px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><td class=\"desc\" style=\"background-color:rgb(251,250,249);border-style:solid;border-width:0px;color:rgb(14,107,145);margin:0px;padding:0px;text-align:center;\">A glimpse of the northern region of Vũng Tàu.</td></tr></tbody></table></figure><p>&nbsp;</p></div><p style=\"background-color:transparent;color:rgb(0,0,0);list-style-type:none;margin:0px 0px 25px;padding:0px;text-align:justify;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;list-style-type:none;margin:0px;padding:0px;\">A serene charm harmonizing with vibrant life</strong></p><p style=\"background-color:transparent;color:rgb(0,0,0);list-style-type:none;margin:0px 0px 25px;padding:0px;text-align:justify;\">The coastal area of northern Vũng Tàu enjoys a unique advantage in terms of topography and natural scenery, possessing both forest and sea. According to Luxury Travel Magazine, alongside the development of Vũng Tàu city, the northern part emerges with its distinctive allure, where tranquility and peace by the bay blend with the vibrant modern lifestyle. Notably, the appearance of this area is undergoing significant transformation with the presence of various tourism projects within the Vega City Vũng Tàu complex, creating a lively and attractive atmosphere for visitors.</p><p style=\"background-color:transparent;color:rgb(0,0,0);list-style-type:none;margin:0px 0px 25px;padding:0px;text-align:justify;\">&quot;Currently, the traditional coastal tourism model - defined as luxurious, secluded resorts - is gradually shifting towards open spaces, incorporating vibrant and intimate activities where life, local culture, and natural landscapes harmonize. This is clearly evident in Vũng Tàu,&quot; the author observes.</p><p style=\"background-color:transparent;color:rgb(0,0,0);list-style-type:none;margin:0px 0px 25px;padding:0px;text-align:justify;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;list-style-type:none;margin:0px;padding:0px;\">The imprint of local culture</strong></p><p style=\"background-color:transparent;color:rgb(0,0,0);list-style-type:none;margin:0px 0px 25px;padding:0px;text-align:justify;\">The distinctive hallmark of the northern Vũng Tàu destination is its connection to folk and local culture. The Manila Times mentions the Đó Theater and describes it as an iconic structure that connects regional folk culture with modern stage technology. Located by the bay of Vũng Tàu, the Đó Theater draws architectural inspiration from the Đó - a traditional fishing tool of the Vietnamese people. The performances serve as a bridge connecting ethnic identity with modern expression. The cultural heritage is vividly showcased, creating allure and spreading the values of identity to the community and international visitors. This venue affirms its position as a hub for major cultural and artistic events both domestically and internationally.</p><div style=\"background-color:transparent;font-size:20px;list-style-type:none;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><figure class=\"table\" style=\"width:702.328px;\"><table class=\"image center\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse;margin:0px auto 10px;max-width:100%;padding:0px;text-align:center;\" align=\"center\"><tbody style=\"list-style-type:none;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><tr style=\"border-style:solid;border-width:0px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><td style=\"border-style:solid;border-width:0px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><div class=\"new\" style=\"background-color:transparent;font-size:20px;list-style-type:none;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><div class=\"new\" style=\"background-color:transparent;font-size:20px;list-style-type:none;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><img class=\"image_resized\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1422/1024;height:auto;list-style-type:none;margin:0px;max-width:100%;padding:0px;width:702.328px;\" src=\"https://baokhanhhoa.vn/file/e7837c02857c8ca30185a8c39b582c03/052026/copilot_20260526_211851_20260526212043.png\" alt=\"copilot_20260526_211851_20260526212043.png\" width=\"1422\" height=\"1024\"></div></div></td></tr><tr style=\"border-style:solid;border-width:0px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><td class=\"desc\" style=\"background-color:rgb(251,250,249);border-style:solid;border-width:0px;color:rgb(14,107,145);margin:0px;padding:0px;text-align:center;\">Đó Theater.</td></tr></tbody></table></figure></div><p style=\"background-color:transparent;color:rgb(0,0,0);list-style-type:none;margin:0px 0px 25px;padding:0px;text-align:justify;\">The author describes: A new day in northern Vũng Tàu begins with the shimmering sunrise over the sandy shore, steady jogging steps in rhythm with the sea&#039;s breath, and the alluring aroma of coffee wafting from outdoor cafes… As the sun sets, northern Vũng Tàu dons a different beauty. Families and friends gather together, watching the sunset over the sea, listening to the soothing melodies, and sharing heartfelt conversations... The outdoor dining space featuring local specialties becomes a rendezvous, where the community and visitors connect, creating an intimate and emotional experience...</p><p style=\"background-color:transparent;color:rgb(0,0,0);list-style-type:none;margin:0px 0px 25px;padding:0px;text-align:justify;\">With the robust growth of tourism in Ba Ria - Vung Tau province, along with the stable return of international visitors, the northern region of Vũng Tàu is asserting its position as an attractive destination, offering authentic and vibrant local cultural experiences that allow travelers to naturally and fully appreciate the beauty of this coastal land in Central Vietnam.</p><p style=\"background-color:transparent;color:rgb(0,0,0);list-style-type:none;margin:0px 0px 25px;padding:0px;text-align:justify;\"><span style=\"background-color:rgb(252,250,246);color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:20px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Newsreader, serif;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;text-align:right;word-spacing:0px;\">NHU THAO (Ba Ria - Vung Tau Online)</span>&nbsp;</span></p></div></div>', NULL),
('en_US', 70, 'North Vũng Tàu – where the sea, mountains, corals, and light harmoniously blend', 'Discover the beauty of Northern Vũng Tàu through the lens of photographer Trần Anh Khoa – where the blue sea, Nui Nho Mountain, white sands, golden sunshine, and vibrant coral reefs harmoniously converge. At Ruby 68 Hotel, guests can fully immerse themselves in the splendor of Vũng Tàu in a single day, from the sunrise over the sea to the sunset behind the mountains.', '<p>There is a very different Vũng Tàu in the northern part of the city.</p><p>Not too noisy, not too hurried, North Vũng Tàu embodies a more expansive and pristine beauty: where the blue sea stretches out before you, the distant Nui Nho Mountain stands still, white sand embraces golden sunlight, and colorful coral reefs lie close to the shore like a natural gift reserved for this bay.</p><figure class=\"image\"><img style=\"aspect-ratio:1200/1707;\" src=\"/storage/image-21.png\" alt=\"image-21.png\" width=\"1200\" height=\"1707\"></figure><p>Here, every moment of the day possesses its own unique beauty. In the morning, dawn gradually breaks on the horizon, the first light touches the surface of the sea, awakening the entire Vũng Tàu bay in gentle shades of gold. As evening descends, the sun slowly sets behind the mountain ranges, leaving warm, peaceful, and emotional hues in the sky.</p><figure class=\"image\"><img style=\"aspect-ratio:1600/1030;\" src=\"/storage/image-18.png\" alt=\"image-18.png\" width=\"1600\" height=\"1030\"></figure><p>Through the lens of photographer <strong>Tran Anh Khoa</strong>, North Vũng Tàu appears both majestic and poetic. It is not only beautiful frames of sea and mountains but also the story of light, of nature, of a land whose beauty is sometimes truly felt only when we pause long enough.</p><figure class=\"image\"><img style=\"aspect-ratio:1800/1211;\" src=\"/storage/image-19.png\" alt=\"image-19.png\" width=\"1800\" height=\"1211\"></figure><p>The uniqueness of North Vũng Tàu lies in the rare harmony of multiple layers of scenery. In front is the blue sea and vibrant coral reefs near the shore. In the distance are the rolling mountains. Above is the sky that changes every hour with the sunlight. All together create a vivid picture, where visitors can fully experience the distinctive beauty of Vũng Tàu: fresh, spacious, natural, and full of life.</p><figure class=\"image\"><img style=\"aspect-ratio:2000/1318;\" src=\"/storage/image-20.png\" alt=\"image-20.png\" width=\"2000\" height=\"1318\"></figure><p>Amidst this scenery, <strong>Ruby 68 Hotel</strong> is a special highlight of North Vũng Tàu.</p><figure class=\"image\"><img style=\"aspect-ratio:2916/1490;\" src=\"/storage/image-22.png\" alt=\"image-22.png\" width=\"2916\" height=\"1490\"></figure><p>Not only a resort by the sea, Ruby 68 also possesses a rare advantage: from the same location, guests can witness <strong>the sunrise emerging over the sea</strong> and welcome <strong>the sunset descending behind the mountains</strong>. This is a very unique experience, making each day at Ruby 68 a complete journey of light – starting with the clear hues of the sea in the morning and concluding with the romantic essence of the mountains at dusk.</p><figure class=\"image\"><img style=\"aspect-ratio:2880/2160;\" src=\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1566073771259-6a8506099945?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1600&q=80\" alt=\"img-9762.jpg\" width=\"2880\" height=\"2160\"></figure><p>From Ruby 68, the beauty of Vũng Tàu is not only revealed in the blue of the ocean or the silhouette of Nui Nho Mountain in the distance, but also in every delicate movement of nature. It is when the sea sparkles under the morning sun, when the coral reefs near the shore enliven the waters, when the city gradually brightens in the evening light, and when the sky changes colors in the moments of sunset.</p><figure class=\"image\"><img style=\"aspect-ratio:2048/1388;\" src=\"/storage/image-23.png\" alt=\"image-23.png\" width=\"2048\" height=\"1388\"></figure><p>Thus, North Vũng Tàu is not just a destination to visit, but a place to feel. To feel the beauty of the sea, the steadfastness of the mountains, the brilliance of the golden sun, the clarity of the coral reefs, and the marvelous changes of light in every moment.</p><p>And at Ruby 68 Hotel, all these beauties are captured within a single view.</p><p><strong>Ruby 68 – where you can fully experience the beauty of Vũng Tàu in one day, from sunrise over the sea to sunset behind the mountains.</strong></p>', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1552566626-52f8b828add9?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&h=927&q=80'),
('en_US', 71, 'Golden Hours Promotion at Ruby 68 – Enjoy up to 37% off when booking a 3-star hotel in Vũng Tàu', 'Indulge in the exclusive Golden Hours offer at Ruby 68 Hotel Vũng Tàu. Enjoy discounts of up to 37%, with an additional 5% off for stays of 3 nights or more, along with a Spa voucher worth 250,000 VND, a 10% F&B discount, and a 100,000 VND voucher for Ruby Sky Bar when you book directly on our official website.', '<p>Indulge in a 3-star retreat by the Vũng Tàu bay with the <strong>Golden Hours</strong> – a special offer exclusively for guests who book directly on the official website of Ruby 68 Hotel.</p><figure class=\"image\"><img style=\"aspect-ratio:1672/941;\" src=\"/storage/image-29.png\" alt=\"image-29.png\" width=\"1672\" height=\"941\"></figure><p>During the golden hours each day, guests have the opportunity to receive discounts of up to <strong>37%</strong> when booking directly. Additionally, for stays of <strong>3 nights or more</strong>, guests will receive an additional <strong>5% discount</strong> when using the promotional code:</p><h1>RUBY68SUMMER</h1><p>This is the perfect opportunity to enjoy a world-class 3-star resort experience at the most optimal cost, along with many attractive benefits available only on the hotel\'s official website.</p><h2>Applicable time frame</h2><h3>EVERY DAY</h3><h3>10:00 AM – 1:00 PM</h3><h3>9:00 PM – 12:00 AM</h3><h3>Vietnam Local Time</h3><p>&nbsp;</p><h2>Benefits for direct bookers</h2><p>When booking during the Golden Hours program, guests will receive:</p><p>✓ Room discounts of up to 37%</p><p>✓ An additional 5% off for stays of 3 nights or more</p><p>✓ Spa voucher worth 250,000 VND</p><p>✓ Ruby Sky Bar voucher worth 100,000 VND</p><p>✓ 10% off dining services at the hotel</p><p>✓ Best price guarantee when booking directly on the official website</p><p>&nbsp;</p><h2>Why should you book directly at Ruby 68?</h2><p>Unlike intermediary booking channels, booking directly on the Ruby 68 Hotel website allows guests to access the best promotional rates along with exclusive benefits reserved solely for the hotel’s customers.</p><p>Ruby 68 Hotel is a 3-star hotel by the Vũng Tàu bay featuring 173 luxurious rooms, private balconies, and stunning views of the sea or city, complemented by premium amenities such as an infinity pool, sauna, spa, restaurants, and the Ruby Sky Bar.</p><p>This is the ideal choice for family vacations, couples, business travelers, or those seeking a luxurious relaxation retreat in Vũng Tàu.</p><hr><h2>Instructions for using the RUBY68SUMMER promotional code</h2><p>To receive the Golden Hours offer, please follow these steps:</p><h3>Step 1</h3><p>Visit the official website:</p><p><strong>https://rubyhotel.trip360.vn</strong></p><h3>Step 2</h3><p>Click the button <strong>Book Now</strong>.</p><h3>Step 3</h3><p>The system will redirect you to <strong>the hotel\'s online booking page (Booking Engine)</strong>.</p><figure class=\"image\"><img style=\"aspect-ratio:1870/764;\" src=\"/storage/image-26.png\" alt=\"image-26.png\" width=\"1870\" height=\"764\"></figure><h3>Step 4</h3><p>In the <strong>Promotion Code</strong>field, enter the code:</p><h3>RUBY68SUMMER</h3><p>Then click <strong>Apply</strong> to activate the offer.</p><figure class=\"image\"><img style=\"aspect-ratio:1340/894;\" src=\"/storage/image-27.png\" alt=\"image-27.png\" width=\"1340\" height=\"894\"></figure><h3>Step 5</h3><p>Continue to select your stay dates, number of guests, and desired room type to see the best promotional rates.</p><h3>Step 6</h3><p>Complete your booking and prepare to enjoy a wonderful vacation at Ruby 68 Hotel Vũng Tàu.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><h2>Book today</h2><p>Don\'t miss the Golden Hours program with a limited number of offers available each day.</p><p>Enter the code <strong>RUBY68SUMMER</strong>, book directly on the official website of Ruby 68 Hotel, and enjoy a 3-star vacation at the best price along with many attractive privileges reserved exclusively for direct bookers.</p>', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1414235077428-338989a2e8c0?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&h=927&q=80');
INSERT INTO `posts_translations` (`lang_code`, `posts_id`, `name`, `description`, `content`, `image`) VALUES
('en_US', 72, 'Vũng Tàu has been voted among the top beautiful beaches in Vietnam', 'Discover Vũng Tàu Beach – one of the top 10 most beautiful beaches in Vietnam as voted by Lonely Planet. With its fine white sand, crystal-clear waters, mild climate, and a plethora of exciting experiences, Vũng Tàu is the ideal destination for a beach holiday, family travel, and exploring Vietnam\'s famous bay.', '<h1>Vũng Tàu Beach – A beauty that has earned recognition from Lonely Planet as one of the most beautiful beaches in Vietnam</h1><p>Vũng Tàu has long been known as one of the most beautiful coastal cities in Vietnam. With its long coastline, crystal-clear waters year-round, and a temperate climate, it is always a favorite destination for millions of travelers both domestically and internationally. Recently, the world-famous travel guide <strong>Lonely Planet</strong> has once again named <strong>Vũng Tàu Beach</strong> in the list of <strong>the 10 most beautiful beaches in Vietnam</strong>, while also awarding this place the title of <strong>&quot;Best City Beach&quot;</strong> – the most beautiful urban beach.</p><p>This recognition not only affirms the natural beauty of Vũng Tàu but also reflects the growing allure of this coastal city on the international tourism map.</p><h2>Where the blue sea meets modern life</h2><figure class=\"image\"><img style=\"aspect-ratio:1800/1359;\" src=\"/storage/image-39.png\" alt=\"image-39.png\" width=\"1800\" height=\"1359\"></figure><p>What sets Vũng Tàu Beach apart is the harmonious blend of nature and urban life. Unlike many secluded beaches, Vũng Tàu&#039;s coastline is right in the heart of the city, offering visitors the sensation of just a few steps away from a tranquil retreat to the vibrant life of the coastal city.</p><p>Along the coastline are lush green palm trees, spacious beachfront parks, and clean, beautiful roads, creating an ideal space for strolling, cycling, or simply sitting quietly to admire the sea at any time of the day.</p><p>As the dawn breaks, the sea reflects the first rays of sunshine in brilliant golden hues. By late afternoon, the sunset paints the horizon red, presenting a romantic beauty that many travelers wish to capture in heartfelt photographs.</p><h2>A paradise of beach experiences</h2><figure class=\"image\"><img style=\"aspect-ratio:1585/2048;\" src=\"/storage/image-40.png\" alt=\"image-40.png\" width=\"1585\" height=\"2048\"></figure><p>Not only does Vũng Tàu possess natural beauty, but it is also a destination for outdoor enthusiasts.</p><p>Visitors can choose to swim, paddleboard, jet ski, paraglide, snorkel, or join tours exploring Back Beach Vung Tau. The rich marine ecosystem and clear waters make this place one of Vietnam&#039;s famous diving spots.</p><p>For those who love relaxation, simply spending a morning walking on the soft sand, listening to the sound of the waves, and enjoying the refreshing sea breeze is enough to feel the unique beauty of this coastal city.</p><h2>The four-season beauty of the coastal city</h2><figure class=\"image\"><img style=\"aspect-ratio:2000/1500;\" src=\"/storage/image-41.png\" alt=\"image-41.png\" width=\"2000\" height=\"1500\"></figure><p>One of the reasons Vũng Tàu consistently ranks among the favorite destinations is its favorable weather almost year-round.</p><p>From around February to September, the weather is sunny, the sea is calm, and the waters are clear, making it perfect for relaxation activities as well as exploring the islands. Even in the late months of the year, Vũng Tàu maintains a pleasant temperature, much more comfortable than many other coastal areas, becoming an attractive choice for international travelers in winter.</p><h2>Gateway to exploring Back Beach Vung Tau</h2><figure class=\"image\"><img style=\"aspect-ratio:1500/1698;\" src=\"/storage/image-42.png\" alt=\"image-42.png\" width=\"1500\" height=\"1698\"></figure><p>Vũng Tàu Beach is also the starting point for exploring one of the most beautiful bays in Vietnam.</p><p>From here, visitors can easily reach Hon Mun – a marine reserve famous for its diverse coral ecosystem, Hon Tam with its luxury resorts, Hon Tre, and many other large and small islands that create a stunning natural tapestry of Back Beach Vung Tau.</p><p>Daily boat trips to the islands offer opportunities to experience activities such as diving, fishing, kayaking, or simply enjoying the pristine beauty amidst the blue ocean.</p><h2>Vũng Tàu – A destination for every journey</h2><figure class=\"image\"><img style=\"aspect-ratio:2000/1300;\" src=\"/storage/image-43.png\" alt=\"image-43.png\" width=\"2000\" height=\"1300\"></figure><p>Being chosen by Lonely Planet as one of the most beautiful beaches in Vietnam is a clear testament to the allure of Vũng Tàu Beach in the eyes of international travelers.</p><p>Whether you are seeking a relaxing beach holiday, a family trip, or an adventure exploring nature and local culture, Vũng Tàu can meet your desires with its harmonious beauty of blue sea, pleasant climate, friendly people, and an ever-developing tourism service system.</p><p>Each season of the year, Vũng Tàu Beach showcases its unique beauty. But no matter when you visit, what lingers in the hearts of travelers is the emerald green water, the soft white sand, and the very special sense of tranquility of this beautiful coastal city.</p><p style=\"margin-left:320px;\">                                                                                                Alex Ta</p><p style=\"margin-left:320px;\">                                                                                          Photo: Trần Anh Khoa</p>', NULL);
